{"nature_communications__doi__10_1038_s41467_020_15432_4": "The 'doi' predicate, or Digital Object Identifier (DOI), is a unique alphanumeric string assigned to identify digital content, providing a persistent link to its location on the internet. This ensures that the content can be accurately cited and accessed, even if it moves.|Here is another description: The DOI (Digital Object Identifier) is a unique alphanumeric string assigned to a specific digital object, such as an article, to provide a persistent link for its location on the internet. It ensures that the object can be accurately and consistently cited and accessed, regardless of changes in the web environment."},
{"10_1038_s41467_020_15432_4": "The DOI 10.1038/s41467-020-15432-4 is assigned to an article in NATURE COMMUNICATIONS, serving as a unique identifier to ensure accurate citation and online location of the article.|Here is another description: 10.1038/s41467-020-15432-4 is the specific DOI assigned to a particular article published in NATURE COMMUNICATIONS. This DOI serves as a permanent link to the article, allowing readers to easily access and cite the work, ensuring its discoverability and integrity in the scientific literature."},
{"nature_communications__website__www_nature_com_naturecommunications": "The predicate \"website\" refers to the specific online platform or address where NATURE COMMUNICATIONS can be accessed. This URL serves as the gateway to the journal's content, including articles, editorials, and other resources.|Here is another description: The predicate \"website\" indicates the online platform or digital address where NATURE COMMUNICATIONS can be accessed, providing a direct link to its published content and resources."},
{"www_nature_com_naturecommunications": "www.nature.com/naturecommunications is the official website for NATURE COMMUNICATIONS, providing access to articles, manuscript submission, and information about the journal's scope, editorial board, and policies.|Here is another description: www.nature.com/naturecommunications is the official website for NATURE COMMUNICATIONS, where readers can access articles, submit manuscripts, and find information about the journal.|Here is another description: www.nature.com/naturecommunications is the official website for the NATURE COMMUNICATIONS journal, where readers can access articles, submit manuscripts, and find information about the journal's scope and editorial policies."},
{"article": "The subject, ARTICLE, refers to a scholarly piece of writing that has been submitted and accepted for publication in a scientific journal. This article likely contains original research, findings, or reviews within a specific field of study.|Here is another description: The subject, ARTICLE, refers to a specific publication within the journal Nature Communications. This article is part of a series of scholarly works published by the journal, which is known for its high-impact research across various scientific disciplines."},
{"article__published_in__nature_communications": "The predicate, published_in, indicates the action or process by which the ARTICLE has been officially released and made available to the public through a specific journal. This process involves peer review, editing, and formatting to meet the journal's standards."},
{"article__doi__https_doi_org_10_1038_s41467_020_15432_4": "The predicate, doi, stands for Digital Object Identifier. It is a unique alphanumeric string assigned to provide a persistent link to its location on the Internet. This identifier is crucial for accurately citing and locating the specific article in digital archives."},
{"cardiovascular_diseases": "Cardiovascular diseases encompass a range of conditions that affect the heart and blood vessels, including coronary artery disease, heart failure, and stroke. These conditions are a major global health concern due to their prevalence and impact on mortality rates.|Here is another description: Cardiovascular diseases encompass a range of disorders that affect the heart or blood vessels, including conditions such as coronary artery disease, heart failure, and stroke. These diseases are a major global health concern due to their high prevalence and significant impact on morbidity and mortality."},
{"cardiovascular_diseases__are__the_leading_cause_of_death_worldwide": "The predicate 'are' establishes the relationship between cardiovascular diseases and their status as the leading cause of death worldwide, highlighting the significant impact these diseases have on global mortality."},
{"the_leading_cause_of_death_worldwide": "The leading cause of death worldwide refers to the primary factor contributing to mortality across the globe. Cardiovascular diseases hold this position due to their high prevalence and the severe health complications they cause, making them a critical area of focus for public health initiatives."},
{"electrocardiogram_ecg": "The Electrocardiogram (ECG) is a diagnostic tool that records the electrical activity of the heart over a period of time using electrodes placed on the skin. It is used to detect abnormalities in heart rhythm and to diagnose various heart conditions."},
{"electrocardiogram_ecg__is__a_major_tool_in_the_diagnoses_of_cardiovascular_diseases": "The predicate 'is' in this context signifies the role or function that the Electrocardiogram (ECG) plays in the field of cardiovascular disease diagnosis. It indicates that the ECG serves as a critical instrument for identifying and assessing heart-related conditions."},
{"a_major_tool_in_the_diagnoses_of_cardiovascular_diseases": "A major tool in the diagnoses of cardiovascular diseases refers to the significant role that the Electrocardiogram (ECG) plays in identifying and assessing conditions related to the heart and blood vessels. It is a key diagnostic method used by healthcare professionals to detect abnormalities and make informed decisions about patient care."},
{"ecgs": "ECGs, or electrocardiograms, are a critical diagnostic tool used to evaluate the electrical activity of the heart. They are widely employed in various clinical settings to detect a range of cardiac conditions, from arrhythmias to hypertrophy."},
{"ecgs__transitioned_from__analog_to_digital": "The transition from analog to digital refers to the shift in technology used to record and analyze ECGs. This change has enabled more advanced computer analysis and automation in the interpretation of ECG data."},
{"analog_to_digital": "The transition from analog to digital in ECGs signifies a move from traditional paper-based recordings to digital formats. This shift allows for greater accessibility, storage, and analysis of ECG data, facilitating more accurate and efficient diagnosis of cardiovascular conditions."},
{"automated_computer_analysis_of_standard_12_lead_electrocardiograms": "Automated computer analysis of standard 12-lead electrocardiograms refers to the use of computer algorithms to interpret and analyze the data obtained from a 12-lead ECG, which is a common diagnostic test used to assess heart functioning by recording the electrical activity of the heart from 12 different angles."},
{"automated_computer_analysis_of_standard_12_lead_electrocardiograms__gained_importance_in__the_process_of_medical_diagnosis": "The phrase 'gained importance in' indicates a growing recognition and reliance on automated computer analysis of 12-lead ECGs within a specific context or process, highlighting its increasing value and integration into clinical practices for enhancing diagnostic capabilities."},
{"the_process_of_medical_diagnosis": "The process of medical diagnosis involves the identification of a disease, condition, or injury based on the signs and symptoms a patient exhibits, as well as the results from various diagnostic tests. In the context of cardiovascular diseases, this process is critical for timely and accurate treatment."},
{"classical_algorithms": "Classical algorithms refer to traditional computational methods used for various tasks, including medical diagnosis. In the context of electrocardiogram (ECG) analysis, these algorithms have been employed to interpret ECG tracings and assist in the diagnosis of cardiovascular diseases.|Here is another description: Classical algorithms refer to traditional computational methods used for analyzing and interpreting electrocardiograms (ECGs). These algorithms have been employed for many years to assist in the diagnosis of cardiovascular diseases by processing the electrical activity of the heart recorded in ECGs.|Here is another description: Classical algorithms refer to traditional computational methods used for analyzing and interpreting electrocardiograms (ECGs). These algorithms have been employed for many years in the medical field to assist in the diagnosis of cardiovascular diseases."},
{"classical_algorithms__have__limited_performance": "The predicate \"have\" in this context signifies the possession or characteristic of a certain quality by classical algorithms. Specifically, it indicates that classical algorithms possess a particular attribute related to their performance in ECG analysis."},
{"limited_performance": "Limited performance in this context refers to the constrained effectiveness or capability of classical algorithms when applied to the automated analysis of electrocardiograms (ECGs). Despite their use in medical diagnosis, these algorithms fall short in providing accurate and reliable results compared to more advanced methods like deep neural networks (DNNs)."},
{"classical_algorithms__precludes_its_usage_as__a_standalone_diagnostic_tool": "The phrase \"precludes its usage as\" indicates a limitation or restriction that prevents classical algorithms from being used in a certain way. In this context, it means that the performance of classical algorithms is insufficient for them to be used independently as a diagnostic tool."},
{"a_standalone_diagnostic_tool": "A standalone diagnostic tool is a device or system that can independently perform medical diagnoses without the need for additional input or interpretation by a human specialist. In the context of ECG analysis, a standalone diagnostic tool would be capable of accurately interpreting ECG results and providing a diagnosis on its own."},
{"classical_algorithms__relegates_them_to__an_ancillary_role": "The phrase \"relegates them to\" indicates a reduction in the importance or primary role of classical algorithms in the context of ECG analysis. It suggests that these algorithms are no longer considered the primary or most effective tool for ECG interpretation."},
{"an_ancillary_role": "An ancillary role describes a secondary or supportive function. In this context, it means that classical algorithms are now considered supplementary to more advanced methods, such as deep neural networks, in the analysis and diagnosis of ECGs."},
{"deep_neural_networks_dnns": "Deep neural networks (DNNs) are advanced machine learning models that consist of multiple layers of interconnected nodes, designed to process and analyze complex data patterns.|Here is another description: Deep neural networks (DNNs) are advanced machine learning models that have shown significant success in various complex tasks such as image classification and speech recognition."},
{"deep_neural_networks_dnns__have_achieved__striking_success_in_tasks_such_as_image_classification_and_speech_recognition": "The phrase \"have achieved\" indicates that deep neural networks have successfully accomplished significant milestones in specific applications, demonstrating their effectiveness and potential in these areas."},
{"striking_success_in_tasks_such_as_image_classification_and_speech_recognition": "Striking success in tasks such as image classification and speech recognition refers to the remarkable performance and accuracy that deep neural networks have demonstrated in analyzing and interpreting visual and auditory data, outperforming traditional algorithms and, in some cases, human experts."},
{"deep_neural_networks_dnns__are_expected_to_improve__health_care_and_clinical_practice": "The expectation is that DNNs will enhance the capabilities and outcomes in health care and clinical practice, potentially surpassing traditional methods in accuracy and efficiency."},
{"health_care_and_clinical_practice": "Health care and clinical practice encompass the diagnosis, treatment, and management of patients' health conditions, which could be significantly improved by the integration of advanced technologies like DNNs."},
{"supervised_learning_models": "Supervised learning models are a type of machine learning algorithm that learn to map an input to an output based on example input-output pairs. They are designed to improve their performance over time as they are exposed to more data."},
{"supervised_learning_models__have_achieved_better_performance_than__a_human_specialist_on_their_routine_work_flow_in_diagnosing_breast_cancer_and_detecting_retinal_diseases": "The predicate \"have achieved better performance than\" indicates that supervised learning models have demonstrated superior results in specific tasks when compared to human specialists. This suggests that these models have reached a level of accuracy and efficiency that surpasses traditional human-based methods in certain applications."},
{"a_human_specialist_on_their_routine_work_flow_in_diagnosing_breast_cancer_and_detecting_retinal_diseases": "A human specialist on their routine work-flow in diagnosing breast cancer and detecting retinal diseases refers to medical professionals who typically perform these diagnostic tasks as part of their regular duties. These specialists use their expertise and experience to analyze medical images and other data to make accurate diagnoses."},
{"training_dnns": "Training DNNs refers to the process of teaching deep neural networks to perform specific tasks, such as image classification, speech recognition, or medical diagnosis, by adjusting their internal parameters based on example input-output pairs."},
{"training_dnns__introduces_the_need_for__large_quantities_of_labeled_data": "Introduces the need for signifies that the process of training deep neural networks (DNNs) necessitates certain requirements or conditions to be met in order to achieve effective and accurate results."},
{"large_quantities_of_labeled_data": "Large quantities of labeled data refer to extensive datasets that contain input examples paired with their corresponding correct outputs, which are essential for training supervised learning models like DNNs to learn the mapping between inputs and outputs."},
{"labeled_data_for_medical_applications": "Labeled data for medical applications refers to datasets that have been annotated or classified for use in training machine learning models, specifically within the healthcare sector. These datasets are crucial for developing algorithms that can automate diagnosis and improve clinical practice."},
{"labeled_data_for_medical_applications__introduce_several_challenges_including__those_related_to_confidentiality_and_security_of_personal_health_information": "The phrase \"introduce several challenges, including\" signifies that the process of obtaining and using labeled data in medical applications is fraught with various difficulties. These challenges must be addressed to effectively implement machine learning models in healthcare settings."},
{"those_related_to_confidentiality_and_security_of_personal_health_information": "The challenges related to confidentiality and security of personal health information involve ensuring that sensitive patient data is protected from unauthorized access and breaches. This is critical in maintaining patient trust and complying with regulations such as HIPAA."},
{"a_preliminary_study": "A preliminary study refers to an initial investigation or research effort aimed at exploring the potential of deep neural networks (DNNs) in the analysis of electrocardiograms (ECGs). This study was conducted to evaluate the effectiveness of DNNs in matching or surpassing the performance of state-of-the-art algorithms and practicing cardiologists in ECG interpretation."},
{"a_preliminary_study__was_presented_in__ref_15": "The phrase \"was presented in\" indicates that the findings or results of the preliminary study were shared or published in a specific reference, in this case, ref. [15]. This predicate signifies the source or medium through which the study's outcomes were communicated to the scientific community or the public."},
{"ref_15": "Ref. [15] is a reference to a specific publication or document where the preliminary study on the use of DNNs in ECG analysis was presented. This reference serves as the source material for the study's details, methodology, results, and conclusions, allowing other researchers or interested parties to access and review the original work."},
{"dnns_for_single_lead_ecgs": "Deep Neural Networks (DNNs) designed for analyzing single-lead Electrocardiograms (ECGs), which are a type of medical diagnostic tool that records the electrical activity of the heart through electrodes attached to the skin.|Here is another description: Deep Neural Networks (DNNs) designed for analyzing single-lead Electrocardiograms (ECGs) represent a cutting-edge approach in medical diagnostics. These networks are specifically tailored to interpret the electrical activity of the heart from a single ECG lead, aiming to automate and enhance the diagnostic process."},
{"dnns_for_single_lead_ecgs__could_match__state_of_the_art_algorithms_when_trained_in_openly_available_datasets": "The capability of DNNs for single-lead ECGs to achieve performance levels comparable to existing advanced algorithms, specifically when these networks are trained using datasets that are freely accessible to the public."},
{"state_of_the_art_algorithms_when_trained_in_openly_available_datasets": "State-of-the-art algorithms represent the most advanced and effective methods currently available for a particular task, in this case, the analysis of ECG data. When DNNs are trained on openly available datasets, they have the potential to reach the performance levels of these leading algorithms."},
{"dnns_for_single_lead_ecgs__present_superior_performance_when_compared_to__practicing_cardiologists_for_a_large_enough_training_dataset": "The phrase \"present superior performance when compared to\" indicates a comparative evaluation where DNNs for single-lead ECGs are assessed against the diagnostic capabilities of human experts, specifically practicing cardiologists. This comparison is based on the accuracy and efficiency of diagnosis under certain conditions."},
{"practicing_cardiologists_for_a_large_enough_training_dataset": "Practicing cardiologists, when equipped with a large enough training dataset, serve as the benchmark for evaluating the performance of DNNs in ECG analysis. These professionals are trained to interpret complex ECG data, diagnose cardiac conditions, and make clinical decisions based on their expertise and the information provided by the ECG."},
{"the_application_of_dnns_in_ecg_analysis": "The application of deep neural networks (DNNs) in electrocardiogram (ECG) analysis represents a cutting-edge approach to automating the diagnosis of cardiovascular diseases. This method leverages the power of machine learning to interpret ECG data, potentially enhancing diagnostic accuracy and efficiency."},
{"the_application_of_dnns_in_ecg_analysis__is_still_an_open_question_if_it_would_be_useful_in__a_realistic_clinical_setting_where_12_lead_ecgs_are_the_standard_technique": "The predicate \"is still an open question if it would be useful in\" reflects the uncertainty and ongoing debate regarding the practical application and effectiveness of DNNs in real-world clinical environments. It highlights the need for further research and validation to determine whether this technology can meet the rigorous standards required for clinical use."},
{"a_realistic_clinical_setting_where_12_lead_ecgs_are_the_standard_technique": "A realistic clinical setting where 12-lead ECGs are the standard technique refers to the typical environment in which ECGs are performed and interpreted by healthcare professionals. In these settings, 12-lead ECGs are used to provide a comprehensive evaluation of cardiac electrical activity, making the integration of DNNs a potentially transformative advancement if proven effective."},
{"short_duration_standard_12_lead_ecg_s12l_ecg": "The short-duration, standard, 12-lead ECG (S12L-ECG) is a diagnostic tool used to evaluate the heart's electrical activity. It is a common procedure performed in various clinical settings, from primary care centers to intensive care units."},
{"short_duration_standard_12_lead_ecg_s12l_ecg__is__the_most_commonly_used_complementary_exam_for_the_evaluation_of_the_heart": "The predicate \"is\" in this context signifies the role or status of the S12L-ECG as the most commonly used complementary exam for heart evaluation. It highlights the widespread adoption and reliance on this method in clinical practice."},
{"the_most_commonly_used_complementary_exam_for_the_evaluation_of_the_heart": "The most commonly used complementary exam for the evaluation of the heart refers to the S12L-ECG's status as a primary tool in assessing cardiac electrical activity. This includes diagnosing arrhythmias, conduction disturbances, acute coronary syndromes, and other cardiac conditions."},
{"s12l_ecg": "The S12L-ECG is a standard 12-lead electrocardiogram, which is a widely used diagnostic tool in various clinical settings, from primary care to intensive care units. It is crucial for evaluating heart conditions and is often performed in environments where specialist cardiologists may not be readily available.|Here is another description: The S12L-ECG is a standard, short-duration, 12-lead electrocardiogram commonly used in various clinical settings to evaluate heart function. It is a crucial diagnostic tool that provides comprehensive information about the heart's electrical activity."},
{"s12l_ecg__can_provide_a_full_evaluation_of__cardiac_electrical_activity": "The capability of the S12L-ECG to provide a full evaluation refers to its comprehensive assessment of various aspects of heart function. This includes detecting arrhythmias, conduction disturbances, acute coronary syndromes, and other cardiac conditions, making it a vital tool in diagnosing and monitoring heart health."},
{"cardiac_electrical_activity": "Cardiac electrical activity encompasses the electrical signals generated by the heart as it contracts and relaxes. This activity is crucial for maintaining the heart's rhythm and overall function. Evaluating this activity through methods like the S12L-ECG helps in diagnosing various heart conditions and monitoring the effects of treatments or other factors on heart function."},
{"s12l_ecg__can_provide_information_about__arrhythmias_conduction_disturbances_acute_coronary_syndromes_cardiac_chamber_hypertrophy_and_enlargement_and_the_effects_of_drugs_and_electrolyte_disturbances": "The S12L-ECG can provide detailed information about various cardiac conditions and abnormalities. This capability allows healthcare professionals to diagnose and monitor a wide range of heart-related issues effectively."},
{"arrhythmias_conduction_disturbances_acute_coronary_syndromes_cardiac_chamber_hypertrophy_and_enlargement_and_the_effects_of_drugs_and_electrolyte_disturbances": "Arrhythmias, conduction disturbances, acute coronary syndromes, cardiac chamber hypertrophy and enlargement, and the effects of drugs and electrolyte disturbances are various cardiac conditions and abnormalities that the S12L-ECG can help identify and monitor. These conditions are critical in diagnosing and managing heart diseases."},
{"s12l_ecgs": "S12L-ECGs, or short-duration, standard, 12-lead electrocardiograms, are a common diagnostic tool used across various clinical settings to evaluate cardiac electrical activity, including arrhythmias, conduction disturbances, and acute coronary syndromes.|Here is another description: S12L-ECGs are a type of electrocardiogram used in the study, specifically analyzed for research purposes. These ECGs provide detailed cardiac electrical activity recordings, crucial for diagnosing various heart conditions."},
{"s12l_ecgs__are_often_performed_in_settings_where_there_are_no_specialists_to_analyze_and_interpret_the_ecg_tracings__primary_care_centers_and_emergency_units": "S12L-ECGs are frequently conducted in environments where specialized medical professionals for ECG analysis and interpretation are not readily available, highlighting the need for automated systems to assist in diagnosis."},
{"primary_care_centers_and_emergency_units": "Primary care centers and emergency units are healthcare facilities where S12L-ECGs are commonly performed. These settings often lack specialists trained in detailed ECG interpretation, making them ideal locations for the implementation of automated ECG analysis technologies."},
{"primary_care_and_emergency_department_health_professionals": "Primary care and emergency department health professionals are medical practitioners who work in initial healthcare settings and urgent care environments, respectively. They are the first point of contact for patients seeking medical attention and are responsible for diagnosing and treating a wide range of health conditions."},
{"primary_care_and_emergency_department_health_professionals__have__limited_diagnostic_abilities_in_interpreting_s12_ecgs": "The predicate 'have' in this context signifies the possession or characteristic of a certain capability or limitation. It indicates that the subject, primary care and emergency department health professionals, possess a specific attribute related to their diagnostic skills."},
{"limited_diagnostic_abilities_in_interpreting_s12_ecgs": "Limited diagnostic abilities in interpreting S12-ECGs refer to the constrained proficiency of primary care and emergency department health professionals in accurately analyzing and understanding the results of standard 12-lead electrocardiograms. This limitation is due to the complexity of ECG interpretation and the lack of specialized training in this area for general healthcare providers."},
{"the_need_for_an_accurate_automatic_interpretation_of_s12l_ecgs": "The need for an accurate automatic interpretation of S12L-ECGs arises from the critical role these tests play in diagnosing a wide range of cardiac conditions, especially in settings where specialist cardiologists are scarce."},
{"the_need_for_an_accurate_automatic_interpretation_of_s12l_ecgs__is_most_acute_in__low_and_middle_income_countries": "The predicate \"is most acute in\" signifies a heightened necessity or urgency for accurate automatic interpretation of S12L-ECGs, particularly in environments where the demand for such technology is greatest due to limited access to specialized medical expertise."},
{"low_and_middle_income_countries": "Low and middle-income countries face significant challenges in healthcare, including a high burden of cardiovascular diseases and limited access to specialist care. This makes the development and implementation of advanced diagnostic tools, like automated S12L-ECG interpretation systems, critically important in these regions.|Here is another description: Low and middle-income countries are nations that have a lower level of economic development and income compared to high-income countries. These countries often face challenges in healthcare infrastructure and access to specialized medical services.|Here is another description: Low and middle-income countries are nations with a gross national income per capita that falls between a specified range, often facing economic challenges and limited resources for healthcare."},
{"low_and_middle_income_countries__are_responsible_for_more_than__75_of_deaths_related_to_cardiovascular_disease": "The phrase \"are responsible for more than\" indicates a significant contribution or accountability. In this context, it highlights the disproportionate impact of cardiovascular disease deaths in low and middle-income countries compared to other regions."},
{"75_of_deaths_related_to_cardiovascular_disease": "75% of deaths related to cardiovascular disease represents a substantial portion of global cardiovascular disease mortality. This statistic underscores the critical need for improved healthcare resources and interventions in low and middle-income countries to address this major public health issue."},
{"low_and_middle_income_countries__often_have__limited_access_to_cardiologists_with_full_expertise_in_ecg_diagnosis": "The phrase 'often have' indicates a common or frequent situation where these countries experience a particular condition or circumstance."},
{"limited_access_to_cardiologists_with_full_expertise_in_ecg_diagnosis": "Limited access to cardiologists with full expertise in ECG diagnosis refers to the scarcity of highly trained medical professionals in these countries who are capable of accurately interpreting electrocardiograms, which are critical for diagnosing heart conditions."},
{"the_use_of_dnns_for_s12l_ecg": "The use of deep neural networks (DNNs) for analyzing standard 12-lead electrocardiograms (S12L-ECG) represents a cutting-edge approach in the field of medical diagnostics, aiming to enhance the accuracy and efficiency of ECG interpretation."},
{"the_use_of_dnns_for_s12l_ecg__is_still_largely_unexplored__due_to_the_shortage_of_full_digital_s12l_ecg_databases": "The exploration of using DNNs for S12L-ECG analysis is currently in its early stages, indicating that there is significant potential for research and development in this area to improve diagnostic outcomes."},
{"due_to_the_shortage_of_full_digital_s12l_ecg_databases": "The shortage of full digital S12L-ECG databases is a critical limitation, as it hampers the ability to train and validate DNNs effectively, thereby slowing down the advancement of automated ECG analysis technologies."},
{"most_available_databases": "Most available databases refer to the collections of electrocardiogram (ECG) recordings that are currently accessible for research and clinical use. These databases are crucial for developing and testing automated analysis algorithms, including deep neural networks."},
{"most_available_databases__comprise__a_few_hundreds_of_tracings_and_no_systematic_annotation_of_the_full_list_of_ecg_diagnoses": "The verb 'comprise' indicates that the subject (most available databases) includes or consists of certain elements. In this context, it means that the databases are made up of a specific number of ECG tracings and lack comprehensive annotations."},
{"a_few_hundreds_of_tracings_and_no_systematic_annotation_of_the_full_list_of_ecg_diagnoses": "A few hundreds of tracings and no systematic annotation of the full list of ECG diagnoses describe the current state of most ECG databases. These databases contain a limited number of ECG recordings and lack detailed, organized annotations for all possible ECG diagnoses, which hinders their utility for training advanced diagnostic algorithms."},
{"the_lack_of_systematically_annotated_data": "The lack of systematically annotated data refers to the absence of comprehensive, organized, and detailed labeling of datasets, particularly in the context of medical applications like ECG analysis. This deficiency arises from the challenges in obtaining large quantities of labeled data due to issues such as confidentiality, security of personal health information, and the labor-intensive nature of annotation."},
{"the_lack_of_systematically_annotated_data__is_unfortunate_as_it_limits__the_usefulness_of_training_datasets_in_a_supervised_learning_setting_for_accurate_automatic_diagnosis_from_s12l_ecg": "The phrase \"is unfortunate as it limits\" describes a situation where the absence of systematically annotated data imposes constraints or reduces the effectiveness of certain processes. In this context, it specifically refers to how the lack of detailed and organized data annotation restricts the potential and performance of training datasets used in supervised learning for medical diagnosis."},
{"the_usefulness_of_training_datasets_in_a_supervised_learning_setting_for_accurate_automatic_diagnosis_from_s12l_ecg": "The usefulness of training datasets in a supervised learning setting for accurate automatic diagnosis from S12L-ECG refers to the effectiveness and reliability of datasets used to train machine learning models, particularly deep neural networks, to accurately interpret and diagnose conditions from standard 12-lead electrocardiograms. These datasets are crucial for achieving high performance in automated ECG analysis, which can significantly impact clinical practice and patient care."},
{"this_paper": "This paper refers to a research document that presents findings and methodologies related to the application of deep neural networks in the field of electrocardiogram analysis. Specifically, it focuses on the use of DNNs for the classification of standard 12-lead electrocardiograms (S12L-ECG).|Here is another description: This paper refers to a scholarly article or research document that presents findings or discussions on a specific topic, in this case, the analysis and classification of S12L-ECG signals. It serves as the source or origin of the information and claims made regarding the effectiveness of a particular method."},
