{"dnns_for_automatic_s12l_ecg_classification": "DNNs for automatic S12L-ECG classification refers to the use of deep neural networks, a subset of machine learning algorithms, to automatically analyze and categorize standard 12-lead electrocardiograms. This technology aims to improve the accuracy and efficiency of ECG interpretation, which is crucial for diagnosing various cardiovascular conditions."},
{"s12l_ecg_exams": "S12L-ECG exams are a specific type of electrocardiogram examination, labeled for detailed analysis and study.|Here is another description: S12L-ECG exams refer to a type of electrocardiogram that is widely used in clinical settings for diagnosing various heart conditions. These exams are characterized by their standard 12-lead configuration, which provides a comprehensive view of the heart's electrical activity from multiple angles."},
