{"dnn__is_developed_to__classify_six_types_of_ecg_abnormalities": "The phrase \"is developed to\" indicates the purpose and functionality of the DNN. It signifies that the DNN has been specifically engineered and trained with the intent to perform a particular task, which in this case is the classification of ECG abnormalities."},
{"classify_six_types_of_ecg_abnormalities": "The classification of six types of ECG abnormalities refers to the DNN's capability to distinguish and categorize different kinds of irregularities found in ECG readings. These abnormalities are representative of both rhythmic (related to the heart's beating pattern) and morphologic (related to the shape and structure of the ECG waves) issues."},
{"ecg_abnormalities": "ECG abnormalities refer to deviations from the normal patterns observed in an electrocardiogram, which is a test that records the electrical activity of the heart. These abnormalities can indicate various heart conditions and are crucial for diagnosis and monitoring."},
