{"1st_degree_av_block_1davb": "The 1st degree AV block (1dAVb) is a type of heart block where the electrical signals between the atria and ventricles are delayed. It is one of the cardiac abnormalities that the DNN is trained to identify from the ECG records."},
{"dnn__trained_to_detect__right_bundle_branch_block_rbbb": "The phrase \"trained to detect\" signifies that the DNN has undergone a learning process where it was exposed to a large dataset of ECG records. Through this training, the network has learned to recognize patterns and features within the ECG signals that are indicative of specific cardiac conditions."},
{"right_bundle_branch_block_rbbb": "Right bundle branch block (RBBB) is a type of heart block where the electrical signals that control the heartbeat are delayed or blocked as they travel through the right bundle branch of the heart's conduction system. This condition can be identified through specific patterns in an ECG, such as a widened QRS complex. The DNN is trained to detect these patterns to diagnose RBBB."},
{"dnn__trained_to_detect__left_bundle_branch_block_lbbb": "The predicate \"trained to detect\" signifies that the DNN has undergone a training process where it learned to recognize and classify specific patterns within ECG data that correspond to certain cardiac conditions. This training involves adjusting the network's parameters based on a large dataset of ECG records to enhance its accuracy in detection."},
{"left_bundle_branch_block_lbbb": "Left bundle branch block (LBBB) is a type of abnormal heart rhythm where the left side of the heart's lower chambers (ventricles) does not contract in sync with the right side. This condition can be identified through specific patterns in an ECG, such as a widened QRS complex, and it is one of the cardiac abnormalities that the DNN is trained to detect."},
{"dnn__trained_to_detect__sinus_bradycardia_sb": "The phrase \"trained to detect\" signifies that the DNN has undergone a learning process where it was exposed to a large dataset of ECG records. Through this training, the network has learned to recognize patterns and features within the ECG data that are indicative of specific cardiac conditions."},
{"sinus_bradycardia_sb": "Sinus bradycardia (SB) is a type of heart rhythm where the heart beats slower than normal. It is characterized by a heart rate below 60 beats per minute in adults and is typically identified through specific patterns observed in an electrocardiogram (ECG). In this context, the DNN has been trained to recognize these patterns and accurately detect the presence of sinus bradycardia in ECG records."},
