{"sinus_tachycardia_st": "Sinus tachycardia (ST) is a condition characterized by an increased heart rate originating from the sinus node, the natural pacemaker of the heart. In the context of the DNN, ST is one of the cardiac abnormalities that the network has been trained to identify from ECG records, highlighting its capability to detect and classify this specific arrhythmia."},
