{"producing_the_dnn_scores_displayed_in_table_2": "The DNN scores displayed in Table 2 are the output results of the deep neural network model's performance evaluation. These scores are generated using the threshold that corresponds to the maximum F1 score for each abnormality, and they are compared against the performances of medical residents and students."},
{"same_dataset": "The same dataset refers to a collection of medical exams used for evaluation purposes, specifically to assess the performance of different groups in identifying abnormalities."},
{"same_dataset__evaluated_by__two_4th_year_cardiology_residents_two_3rd_year_emergency_residents_and_two_5th_year_medical_students": "The phrase \"evaluated by\" indicates the action of assessment or analysis performed by various medical professionals on the dataset to annotate and identify abnormalities."},
{"two_4th_year_cardiology_residents_two_3rd_year_emergency_residents_and_two_5th_year_medical_students": "The object consists of two 4th year cardiology residents, two 3rd year emergency residents, and two 5th year medical students, who are the medical professionals tasked with evaluating and annotating half of the exams in the test set."},
