{"dnn_results_in_table_2": "The DNN results in Table 2 represent the performance metrics of a deep neural network model that was used to evaluate the same dataset as the medical residents and students. These results include precision-recall scores and are compared against the human annotators' performances."},
{"their_precision_recall_scores": "The precision-recall scores refer to the performance metrics of two 4th year cardiology residents, two 3rd year emergency residents, and two 5th year medical students who annotated half of the exams in the test set. These scores are averaged and compared with the results from a deep neural network (DNN)."},
{"their_precision_recall_scores__plotted_in__fig_2": "The phrase 'plotted in' indicates that the precision-recall scores of the medical residents and students have been graphically represented. This plotting allows for a visual comparison of their performance metrics against those of the DNN."},
{"dnn__matches_or_outperforms__medical_residents_and_students_for_all_abnormalities": "The predicate \"matches or outperforms\" indicates a comparative performance evaluation where the DNN's results are measured against those of medical residents and students. This comparison is based on the F1 score, a metric that balances precision and recall, showing the DNN's effectiveness in identifying abnormalities."},
{"medical_residents_and_students_for_all_abnormalities": "Medical residents and students represent the human benchmark in this evaluation. They are in various stages of their medical training, with 4th year cardiology residents, 3rd year emergency residents, and 5th year medical students participating in the study. Their performance in detecting abnormalities is averaged and compared to the DNN's performance."},
{"confusion_matrices_and_inter_rater_agreement_kappa_coefficients": "Confusion matrices and inter-rater agreement (kappa coefficients) are statistical tools used to evaluate the performance and reliability of classification models, including those used in medical diagnosis. They help in understanding the accuracy of predictions by comparing them against actual outcomes and assessing the level of agreement between different raters."},
{"confusion_matrices_and_inter_rater_agreement_kappa_coefficients__provided_in__supplementary_tables_1_and_2_a": "The phrase \"provided in\" indicates that the information or data related to the subject (confusion matrices and kappa coefficients) can be found or accessed in a specific location or document. In this context, it directs the reader to Supplementary Tables 1 and 2(a) where detailed data is presented."},
{"supplementary_tables_1_and_2_a": "Supplementary Tables 1 and 2(a) are additional tables included in a research paper or report that provide extra data and details not included in the main text. These tables offer a deeper insight into the study's findings, including specific metrics like confusion matrices and kappa coefficients for different groups of medical professionals and a deep neural network (DNN)."},
