{"supplementary_table_2_b__compares__inter_rater_agreement_between_the_neural_network_and_the_certified_cardiologists": "The predicate \"compares\" indicates an analytical action where two or more entities are evaluated against each other to highlight similarities, differences, or levels of agreement. In this context, it suggests a detailed examination of how closely aligned the assessments or ratings of different groups are."},
{"inter_rater_agreement_between_the_neural_network_and_the_certified_cardiologists": "The inter-rater agreement between the neural network and the certified cardiologists refers to the level of consistency or concordance in the evaluations or diagnoses made by an automated neural network system and human experts (certified cardiologists). This agreement is typically measured using statistical methods such as kappa coefficients, which quantify the degree of agreement beyond what would be expected by chance."},
{"trained_cardiologist": "The trained cardiologist is a medical professional with specialized expertise in cardiology, who is involved in reviewing and analyzing medical errors.|Here is another description: A trained cardiologist is a medical professional who has undergone specialized training in cardiology, the study and treatment of heart diseases. In this context, the cardiologist is involved in reviewing and analyzing errors made by a deep neural network (DNN), medical residents, and students."},
{"trained_cardiologist__reviewed__mistakes_made_by_the_dnn_medical_residents_and_students": "The action of reviewing involves carefully examining and assessing the mistakes made by various individuals, including a DNN, medical residents, and students, to understand the source of the errors."},
{"mistakes_made_by_the_dnn_medical_residents_and_students": "The mistakes made by the DNN, medical residents, and students are the errors or inaccuracies in medical assessments or diagnoses that were identified and reviewed by the trained cardiologist."},
