{"source_of_the_error": "The \"source of the error\" refers to the underlying cause or origin of the mistakes made by the DNN, medical residents, and students. In this context, identifying the source of the error is crucial for improving diagnostic accuracy and understanding the limitations of both human and machine-based medical assessments.|Here is another description: The object represents the identified cause or origin of the errors made in the medical diagnoses by the DNN, residents, and students, which was the focus of their collaborative analysis and agreement."},
{"cardiologist": "The cardiologist in this context is a trained medical professional specializing in cardiology, who reviewed errors made by a Deep Neural Network (DNN), medical residents, and students. Their role involved analyzing and explaining the sources of these errors.|Here is another description: The cardiologist in this context is a certified medical professional specialized in diagnosing and treating heart conditions. They are involved in the manual labeling of medical reports as part of a classification process.|Here is another description: The cardiologist in this context is a certified medical professional specialized in diagnosing and treating heart conditions. They are responsible for reviewing and interpreting medical reports to identify abnormalities."},
