{"the_medical_students_for_many_abnormalities": "The medical students for many abnormalities represent a group with potentially higher or more consistent accuracy in diagnosing ECG abnormalities compared to emergency residents. This comparison highlights differences in training, experience, or frequency of practice in interpreting ECGs."},
{"the_fact_that_emergency_residents_unlike_cardiology_residents_do_not_have_to_interpret_these_exams_on_a_daily_basis": "The subject refers to the observation that emergency residents, in contrast to cardiology residents, are not required to interpret ECG exams daily."},
{"the_fact_that_emergency_residents_unlike_cardiology_residents_do_not_have_to_interpret_these_exams_on_a_daily_basis__might_justify__why_the_performance_of_the_emergency_residents_is_worse_than_the_medical_students": "The predicate suggests a possible explanation or rationale for a certain situation or outcome, in this case, it is used to propose a reason for the difference in performance between emergency residents and medical students."},
