{"medical_students": "Medical students are individuals who are currently enrolled in a medical school program, undergoing training to become licensed physicians. They are in the process of acquiring comprehensive knowledge and skills in various medical disciplines, including cardiology, through both theoretical studies and practical experiences.|Here is another description: Medical students are individuals who are enrolled in a medical school program and are in the process of obtaining their medical degree. They are typically involved in various stages of medical training, including clinical rotations, practical exercises, and research projects.|Here is another description: Medical students are individuals who are enrolled in a medical school program and are in the process of obtaining a medical degree. They are typically engaged in various educational activities, including clinical rotations, coursework, and practical training under the supervision of experienced medical professionals.|Here is another description: Medical students are individuals enrolled in a medical school program, undergoing training to become medical doctors. In this context, they were tasked with manually reviewing ECGs using a diagnostic system, under the guidance of a certified cardiologist."},
