{"ecg_rhythm_and_morphological_abnormalities_in_clinical_s12l_ecg_exams": "ECG rhythm and morphological abnormalities in clinical S12L-ECG exams refer to the various irregular patterns and structural deviations that can be detected in a standard 12-lead electrocardiogram. These abnormalities may indicate underlying cardiac conditions that require medical attention."},
{"proof_of_concept_study": "The proof-of-concept study refers to an initial research project aimed at demonstrating the feasibility of using a deep neural network (DNN) to accurately recognize ECG rhythm and morphological abnormalities in clinical S12L-ECG exams."},
