{"choice_of_architecture_and_hyperparameters": "The choice of architecture and hyperparameters refers to the selection of specific configurations and parameters for a machine learning model, which in this context includes options like the number of residual blocks, kernel size, batch size, learning rate, optimization algorithms, activation functions, and dropout rate."},
{"choice_of_architecture_and_hyperparameters__done_together_with__improvements_in_the_dataset": "\"Done together with\" indicates that the process of selecting the architecture and hyperparameters was carried out concurrently with another activity. In this case, it was done alongside making improvements to the dataset, suggesting an integrated approach where both model configuration and data enhancement were considered simultaneously."},
