{"hyperparameters": "The hyperparameters refer to the various configuration settings used in the training of neural networks, which significantly influence the model's performance and efficiency. These settings include parameters like the number of residual blocks, kernel size, batch size, learning rate, optimization algorithms, activation functions, and dropout rates."},
{"hyperparameters__chosen_among__options_residual_neural_networks_with_2_4_8_16_residual_blocks_kernel_size_8_16_32_batch_size_16_32_64_initial_learning_rate_0_01_0_001_0_0001_optimization_algorithms_sgd_adam_activation_functions_relu_elu_dropout_rate_0_0_5_0_8_number_of_epochs_without_improvement_in_plateaus_between_5_and_10_that_would_result_in_a_reduction_in_the_learning_rate_between_0_1_and_0_5": "The phrase \"chosen among\" indicates the process of selecting specific hyperparameter settings from a predefined set of options. This selection is critical as it determines the architecture and behavior of the neural network during training."},
{"options_residual_neural_networks_with_2_4_8_16_residual_blocks_kernel_size_8_16_32_batch_size_16_32_64_initial_learning_rate_0_01_0_001_0_0001_optimization_algorithms_sgd_adam_activation_functions_relu_elu_dropout_rate_0_0_5_0_8_number_of_epochs_without_improvement_in_plateaus_between_5_and_10_that_would_result_in_a_reduction_in_the_learning_rate_between_0_1_and_0_5": "The options for hyperparameters include residual neural networks with varying numbers of residual blocks (2, 4, 8, 16), different kernel sizes (8, 16, 32), batch sizes (16, 32, 64), initial learning rates (0.01, 0.001, 0.0001), optimization algorithms (SGD, ADAM), activation functions (ReLU, ELU), dropout rates (0, 0.5, 0.8), and conditions for reducing the learning rate based on the number of epochs without improvement."},
{"procedure__tried_to__use_vectorcardiogram_linear_transformation_to_reduce_the_dimensionality_of_the_input": "The phrase \"tried to\" indicates an experimental approach within the procedure, where various techniques and modifications were attempted to enhance the model. This involves testing different methods to see which would yield the best results in terms of model accuracy and efficiency."},
{"use_vectorcardiogram_linear_transformation_to_reduce_the_dimensionality_of_the_input": "Using vectorcardiogram linear transformation to reduce the dimensionality of the input involves applying a mathematical technique to transform the input data. This transformation aims to simplify the data by reducing its dimensions, which can help in making the machine learning model more efficient and potentially improve its performance by focusing on the most relevant features."},
{"procedure__tried_to__include_lstm_layer_before_convolutional_layers": "The predicate \"tried to\" indicates an attempt or experiment made as part of the procedure to enhance the neural network's performance by modifying its architecture or hyperparameters."},
