{"et_al": "\"et al.\" is a Latin abbreviation for \"et alia,\" which means \"and others.\" In this context, it refers to the other co-authors who, along with D. Hutchison, contributed to the research paper on the evaluation of pooling operations in convolutional architectures."},
{"hutchison_d__published_in__artificial_neural_networks_icann_2010_vol_6354": "The phrase \"published in\" indicates that the work by D. Hutchison and colleagues was presented and made available in a specific academic publication, which in this case is the conference proceedings of Artificial Neural Networks\u2014ICANN 2010."},
{"artificial_neural_networks_icann_2010_vol_6354": "Artificial Neural Networks\u2014ICANN 2010 Vol. 6354 is a volume in the series of proceedings from the International Conference on Artificial Neural Networks held in 2010, which includes a collection of papers on various topics related to neural networks, edited by K. Diamantaras et al. and published by Springer."},
{"hutchison_d__published__evaluation_of_pooling_operations_in_convolutional_architectures_for_object_recognition": "The predicate 'published' indicates that D. Hutchison, along with co-authors, has authored and released a scholarly work. This work contributes to the academic and practical understanding of convolutional neural networks, particularly in the context of object recognition."},
{"evaluation_of_pooling_operations_in_convolutional_architectures_for_object_recognition": "The object 'Evaluation of pooling operations in convolutional architectures for object recognition' is a scholarly article that assesses the effectiveness of different pooling operations within convolutional neural networks. This evaluation aims to enhance the performance of these networks in recognizing objects, contributing valuable insights to the field of machine learning and computer vision."},
{"kingma_d_p": "Kingma, D. P. is a researcher who has contributed to the field of machine learning, particularly in the development of optimization methods for neural networks.|Here is another description: Kingma, D. P. is a researcher who, along with Ba, J., contributed to the field of machine learning by developing a method for stochastic optimization known as Adam.|Here is another description: Kingma, D. P. is a researcher who has contributed to the field of machine learning, particularly in the area of optimization techniques for neural networks."},
{"kingma_d_p__co_authored_with__ba_j": "The predicate \"co-authored with\" indicates a collaborative effort between two or more individuals in the creation of a scientific work, such as a research paper or conference proceeding."},
{"ba_j": "Ba, J. is a researcher who has collaborated with Kingma, D. P. on the development of Adam, a method for stochastic optimization, which was presented at the 3rd International Conference for Learning Representations (ICLR)."},
{"kingma_d_p__published_in__proc_3rd_international_conference_for_learning_representations_iclr": "The predicate \"published in\" indicates that the work or research conducted by Kingma, D. P. and Ba, J. was presented and made available to the scientific community through the proceedings of a specific conference."},
{"proc_3rd_international_conference_for_learning_representations_iclr": "The Proc. 3rd International Conference for Learning Representations (ICLR) is a conference that focuses on advancements in machine learning techniques and theories, providing a platform for researchers to share their findings and innovations in the field."},
{"kingma_d_p__published__adam_a_method_for_stochastic_optimization": "The predicate \"published\" indicates that Kingma, D. P., along with co-author Ba, J., has released a scholarly work detailing a novel method for optimizing neural network training."},
{"adam_a_method_for_stochastic_optimization": "\"Adam: a method for stochastic optimization\" is a research paper presented at the 3rd International Conference for Learning Representations (ICLR) that introduces the Adam optimization algorithm, designed to improve the efficiency and performance of stochastic gradient descent in training machine learning models."},
{"he_k": "He, K. is a researcher who has made significant contributions to the field of computer vision, particularly in the development of deep learning techniques for image classification.|Here is another description: He, K. is a researcher who has made significant contributions to the field of computer vision, particularly in the development of deep learning techniques for image classification.|Here is another description: He, K. is a researcher who has made significant contributions to the field of computer vision, particularly through his work on neural networks and image classification."},
{"he_k__co_authored_with__zhang_x_ren_s_sun_j": "The predicate \"co-authored with\" indicates a collaborative effort between multiple researchers in producing a scientific work. In this case, He, K. worked alongside Zhang, X., Ren, S., and Sun, J. to publish a paper on advancing image classification performance using deep learning methods."},
{"zhang_x_ren_s_sun_j": "Zhang, X., Ren, S., and Sun, J. are co-authors who, along with He, K., contributed to the research and publication of a paper that explores the use of rectifiers in surpassing human-level performance on ImageNet classification. Their combined expertise and collaboration led to significant advancements in the field of computer vision."},
{"he_k__published_in__proc_ieee_international_conference_on_computer_vision": "The predicate \"published in\" indicates that the subject, He, K., has contributed research work that was accepted and presented at a specific academic conference, in this case, the IEEE International Conference on Computer Vision."},
{"proc_ieee_international_conference_on_computer_vision": "Proc. IEEE International Conference on Computer Vision is an academic conference proceeding that publishes cutting-edge research in the field of computer vision, including topics such as image and video analysis, pattern recognition, and machine learning."},
{"he_k__published__delving_deep_into_rectifiers_surpassing_human_level_performance_on_imagenet_classification": "The predicate 'published' indicates that He, K. has authored and released a research paper, contributing new knowledge and findings to the scientific community."},
{"delving_deep_into_rectifiers_surpassing_human_level_performance_on_imagenet_classification": "\"Delving deep into rectifiers: surpassing human-level performance on imagenet classification\" is a research paper authored by He, K. and his colleagues, which presents novel findings on improving the performance of neural networks in image classification tasks, achieving results that exceed human-level accuracy on the ImageNet dataset."},
{"saito_t": "Saito, T. is an author who has contributed to research in the field of binary classifiers, particularly focusing on the evaluation of these classifiers on imbalanced datasets.|Here is another description: Saito, T. is an author who, in collaboration with Rehmsmeier, contributed to a study on the evaluation of binary classifiers, particularly focusing on the effectiveness of precision-recall plots over ROC plots for imbalanced datasets.|Here is another description: Saito, T. is an author who has contributed to the field of machine learning and data analysis, particularly in the evaluation of binary classifiers."},
{"saito_t__co_authored_with__rehmsmeier_m": "The predicate \"co-authored with\" indicates a collaborative effort between two or more individuals in the creation of a scholarly work, in this case, a research paper on the effectiveness of precision-recall plots over ROC plots for evaluating binary classifiers."},
{"rehmsmeier_m": "Rehmsmeier, M. is a collaborator and co-author in the research paper discussing the advantages of precision-recall plots over ROC plots when assessing binary classifiers on datasets with imbalanced class distributions."},
{"saito_t__published_in__plos_one": "The phrase \"published in\" indicates the action of an author or authors releasing their scholarly work in a specific academic journal or conference proceedings, making their research findings accessible to the scientific community."},
{"plos_one": "PLoS ONE is a peer-reviewed, open-access scientific journal that publishes research across all areas of science and medicine. It is known for its broad scope and commitment to making research findings freely available to the public."},
{"saito_t__published__the_precision_recall_plot_is_more_informative_than_the_roc_plot_when_evaluating_binary_classifiers_on_imbalanced_datasets": "The predicate 'published' indicates that Saito, T. has authored and released a scientific work, contributing to the academic and practical understanding of evaluating binary classifiers."},
{"the_precision_recall_plot_is_more_informative_than_the_roc_plot_when_evaluating_binary_classifiers_on_imbalanced_datasets": "The object \"The precision-recall plot is more informative than the ROC plot when evaluating binary classifiers on imbalanced datasets\" is a scientific publication by Saito, T. and Rehmsmeier, M. that discusses the advantages of using precision-recall plots over ROC plots for assessing the performance of binary classifiers, especially in scenarios where the dataset is imbalanced."},
{"this_research": "This research refers to the study or project that is being acknowledged for its funding sources. It involves multiple contributors and is supported by various funding agencies and projects.|Here is another description: This research refers to the study or project that has been conducted and is being acknowledged for its funding sources. It is a comprehensive effort involving multiple contributors and institutions.|Here is another description: This research refers to a scientific study or project that has received financial support from various sources. The acknowledgments section of the research highlights the contributions and funding received from multiple agencies and programs."},
{"this_research__was_partly_supported_by__the_brazilian_agencies_cnpq_capes_and_fapemig": "The phrase \"was partly supported by\" indicates that the research received financial or resource-based assistance from certain entities, but it was not solely dependent on them. This suggests a partial contribution towards the completion or facilitation of the research."},
{"the_brazilian_agencies_cnpq_capes_and_fapemig": "The Brazilian Agencies CNPq, CAPES, and FAPEMIG are organizations that provide financial support for research and education in Brazil. CNPq (National Council for Scientific and Technological Development) funds scientific research, CAPES (Coordination for the Improvement of Higher Education Personnel) supports graduate education, and FAPEMIG (Research Support Foundation of the State of Minas Gerais) funds research in the state of Minas Gerais."},
{"this_research__was_partly_supported_by__projects_iats_masweb_inct_cyber_rede_de_teleassist\u00eancia_de_minas_gerais_and_atmosphere": "The phrase \"was partly supported by\" indicates that the research received financial or resource-based assistance from various sources. This support is not exclusive, meaning there are other contributors not mentioned in this specific acknowledgment."},
{"projects_iats_masweb_inct_cyber_rede_de_teleassist\u00eancia_de_minas_gerais_and_atmosphere": "The objects\u2014projects IATS, MASWeb, INCT-Cyber, Rede de Teleassist\u00eancia de Minas Gerais, and Atmosphere\u2014are specific initiatives or programs that provided partial support to the research. These projects are likely funded by Brazilian Agencies and involve collaboration across different fields or objectives."},
{"this_research__was_partly_supported_by__the_wallenberg_ai_autonomous_systems_and_software_program_wasp_funded_by_knut_and_alice_wallenberg_foundation": "The phrase \"was partly supported by\" indicates that the research received partial financial assistance or funding. This support is crucial for the execution and completion of the research project, allowing the researchers to access necessary resources and conduct their studies."},
{"the_wallenberg_ai_autonomous_systems_and_software_program_wasp_funded_by_knut_and_alice_wallenberg_foundation": "The Wallenberg AI, Autonomous Systems and Software Program (WASP) is a significant funding initiative backed by the Knut and Alice Wallenberg Foundation. WASP aims to advance research and development in the fields of artificial intelligence, autonomous systems, and software, providing financial support to various projects and initiatives in these areas."},
{"we__thank__nvidia_for_awarding_our_project_with_a_titan_v_gpu": "The predicate \"thank\" indicates the action of expressing gratitude or appreciation. In this context, it signifies the researchers' acknowledgment and appreciation for the support they have received."},
{"nvidia_for_awarding_our_project_with_a_titan_v_gpu": "The object \"NVIDIA for awarding our project with a Titan V GPU\" specifies the entity being thanked and the specific support provided. NVIDIA is a technology company known for its graphics processing units (GPUs), and the Titan V GPU is a high-performance computing device that likely aided the research project."},
{"a_l_p_r": "A.L.P.R. is an individual or entity involved in research activities, as indicated by the receipt of scholarships to support their work.|Here is another description: A.L.P.R is an individual who played a key role in the study by being responsible for the study design and acting as the project leader. Their contributions were critical in overseeing the project's direction and ensuring its successful execution.|Here is another description: A.L.P.R is an individual who played a significant role in the study, contributing to the study design and conceiving the project.|Here is another description: A.L.P.R. is an abbreviation for a person or department that is responsible for receiving and processing requests for materials. This entity is identified as the appropriate contact for such inquiries within the given context."},
{"a_l_p_r__receives__unrestricted_research_scholarships_from_cnpq_and_fapemig_ppm": "The predicate \"receives\" indicates the action of being granted or awarded something, in this case, financial support in the form of scholarships."},
{"unrestricted_research_scholarships_from_cnpq_and_fapemig_ppm": "Unrestricted research scholarships from CNPq and FAPEMIG (PPM) are financial awards provided by the Brazilian agencies Conselho Nacional de Desenvolvimento Cient\u00edfico e Tecnol\u00f3gico (CNPq) and Funda\u00e7\u00e3o de Amparo \u00e0 Pesquisa do Estado de Minas Gerais (FAPEMIG) under the Produtividade em Pesquisa (PPM) program, intended to support research activities without specific restrictions on the use of funds."},
{"w_m_jr": "W.M.Jr. is an individual acknowledged in the research for receiving financial support. They are part of a group of researchers who have been awarded various scholarships and grants to support their work."},
{"w_m_jr__receives__an_unrestricted_research_scholarship_from_cnpq": "The predicate \"receives\" indicates the action of being granted or awarded something, in this case, a scholarship. It signifies the transfer of financial support from a funding agency to a researcher to aid in their academic or research endeavors."},
{"an_unrestricted_research_scholarship_from_cnpq": "An unrestricted research scholarship from CNPq is a form of financial aid provided by the Brazilian National Council for Scientific and Technological Development (CNPq) to support research activities without imposing specific restrictions on how the funds can be used. This allows the recipient to utilize the scholarship for a broad range of research-related expenses."},
{"a_h_r": "A.H.R. is an individual who is acknowledged for their involvement in research, supported by various funding agencies and projects. Their contributions are recognized alongside other researchers who receive support from similar sources.|Here is another description: A.H.R is an author who contributed to various aspects of the study, including study design, implementation of the deep neural network, and generation of figures and tables.|Here is another description: A.H.R is one of the contributors to the study, involved in various stages including study design, choosing the architecture of the deep neural network, implementing and tuning it, and conducting statistical analysis of the test data.|Here is another description: A.H.R. is one of the individuals to whom correspondence and requests for materials should be directed. This person is likely a point of contact for further communication or information."},
{"a_h_r__receives__scholarships_from_capes_and_cnpq": "The predicate \"receives\" indicates the action of being granted or awarded financial support or resources. In this context, it signifies the acknowledgment of A.H.R. being provided with scholarships as part of their research support."},
{"scholarships_from_capes_and_cnpq": "The scholarships from CAPES and CNPq are financial awards provided by the Coordination for the Improvement of Higher Education Personnel (CAPES) and the National Council for Scientific and Technological Development (CNPq), respectively. These scholarships are intended to support research activities and are part of the acknowledgments for the research project."},
{"m_h_r_and_d_m_o": "M.H.R. and D.M.O. are individuals who are part of a research project or team, as indicated by their acknowledgment of receiving specific scholarships. Their involvement suggests they are active contributors to the research efforts supported by various funding agencies."},
{"m_h_r_and_d_m_o__receive__google_latin_america_research_award_scholarships": "The predicate \"receive\" indicates the action of being granted or awarded something. In this context, it signifies that M.H.R. and D.M.O. have been awarded scholarships, which are financial aids provided to support their research activities."},
{"google_latin_america_research_award_scholarships": "The Google Latin America Research Award scholarships are financial awards provided by Google to support research initiatives in Latin America. These scholarships are intended to foster and encourage research efforts in the region, providing necessary funding to researchers like M.H.R. and D.M.O."},
{"none_of_the_funding_agencies": "The subject refers to the funding agencies that supported the research, including Brazilian Agencies CNPq, CAPES, and FAPEMIG, projects IATS, MASWeb, INCT-Cyber, Rede de Teleassist\u00eancia de Minas Gerais and Atmosphere, the Wallenberg AI, Autonomous Systems and Software Program (WASP) funded by Knut and Alice Wallenberg Foundation, and NVIDIA."},
