{"12_lead_ecg": "A 12-lead ECG, or electrocardiogram, is a medical test that records the electrical activity of the heart from twelve different angles. It is a standard diagnostic tool used to detect various heart conditions by providing a comprehensive view of the heart's electrical patterns."},
{"automatic_diagnosis_of_the_12_lead_ecg": "The automatic diagnosis of the 12-lead ECG refers to a method or system designed to analyze and interpret the results of a 12-lead electrocardiogram, which is a common diagnostic test that records the electrical activity of the heart from 12 different angles.|Here is another description: The automatic diagnosis of the 12-lead ECG refers to a method or system that uses technology to interpret and diagnose conditions based on the data from a 12-lead electrocardiogram, which is a common diagnostic test in cardiology."},
{"automatic_diagnosis_of_the_12_lead_ecg__uses__a_deep_neural_network": "The term \"uses\" in this context indicates the employment or application of a specific technology or method\u2014in this case, a deep neural network\u2014to perform the task of automatic diagnosis of the 12-lead ECG."},
{"a_deep_neural_network": "A deep neural network is a type of machine learning model inspired by the structure and function of the human brain. It consists of multiple layers of interconnected nodes or neurons, which enable it to learn and make decisions based on complex patterns in data."},
