{"trained_cardiologist": "The trained cardiologist is a medical professional with specialized expertise in cardiology, having undergone extensive training and education in the field. Their role involves diagnosing and treating heart-related conditions, as well as providing guidance and oversight in medical settings.|Here is another description: A trained cardiologist is a medical professional who has undergone specialized training in cardiology, the study and treatment of heart diseases. In this context, the cardiologist is involved in reviewing and analyzing errors made by a deep neural network (DNN), medical residents, and students in a medical setting."},
{"trained_cardiologist__reviewed__mistakes_made_by_the_dnn_medical_residents_and_students": "The action of reviewing involves carefully examining and assessing the mistakes made by others. In this context, the cardiologist is analyzing errors to understand their origins and improve future performance. This process includes discussions and collaboration with medical residents and students to identify and address the sources of these errors."},
{"mistakes_made_by_the_dnn_medical_residents_and_students": "The mistakes made by the DNN, medical residents, and students refer to errors in diagnosis or decision-making processes. These errors are the focus of the cardiologist's review, aimed at understanding the causes and improving the accuracy and reliability of medical diagnoses. The analysis of these mistakes helps in evaluating the performance of different groups and identifying areas for improvement."},
