{"source_of_the_error": "The 'source of the error' refers to the underlying cause or reason why mistakes were made by the DNN, medical residents, and students. Identifying this source is crucial for understanding how to prevent future errors and improve performance in medical diagnostics and treatments.|Here is another description: The object represents the identified cause or origin of the errors made in the medical diagnoses by the DNN, residents, and students, which was the focus of their collaborative analysis and agreement."},
{"cardiologist": "The cardiologist is a trained medical professional specializing in heart-related conditions, who reviewed errors made by others and sought to understand the sources of these errors.|Here is another description: The cardiologist in this context is a certified medical professional specialized in diagnosing and treating heart conditions. They are involved in the process of manually labeling medical reports as part of a training and validation set for a classification model.|Here is another description: The cardiologist in this context is a certified medical professional specialized in diagnosing and treating heart conditions. They are responsible for reviewing and interpreting medical reports to identify abnormalities."},
