{"precision_ppv_recall_sensitivity_specificity_and_f1_score": "Precision (PPV), recall (sensitivity), specificity, and F1 score are standard metrics used to assess the performance of diagnostic tests or models. Precision measures the proportion of true positive results among all positive results, recall (sensitivity) measures the proportion of actual positives that are correctly identified, specificity measures the proportion of negatives that are correctly identified, and the F1 score is the harmonic mean of precision and recall, providing a balance between the two."},
