{"acute_coronary_syndromes_or_cardiac_chamber_enlargements": "Acute coronary syndromes represent a group of heart conditions associated with sudden, reduced blood flow to the heart, while cardiac chamber enlargements refer to the abnormal increase in the size of one or more of the heart's chambers, both of which are significant in the context of ECG diagnosis."},
{"results__cannot_be_extended_to__untested_clinical_situations": "The phrase \"cannot be extended to\" signifies a limitation in the applicability of the study's findings. It indicates that the results, while positive for the tested scenarios, do not guarantee similar performance in other, untested clinical situations."},
