{"in_real_time": "Real-time diagnosis refers to the immediate and continuous evaluation of a patient's condition as data is collected and analyzed. In the context of ECG interpretation, real-time diagnosis would allow for rapid feedback and improvements to the DNN algorithm, ultimately leading to more reliable automatic diagnosis and improved clinical practice."},
{"diagnosis": "The diagnosis refers to the identification of a medical condition or disease based on the analysis of symptoms, signs, and test results. In the context of electrocardiograms (ECGs), diagnosis involves interpreting the electrical activity of the heart to detect abnormalities or diseases.|Here is another description: The diagnosis refers to the identification of an abnormality in a medical context, based on the consensus of multiple sources.|Here is another description: The diagnosis refers to the identification or conclusion about a medical condition based on the analysis of symptoms, tests, and other medical evaluations. In this context, it specifically relates to the detection of an abnormality in medical data.|Here is another description: The diagnosis refers to the medical decision-making process regarding the presence or absence of an abnormality based on the input from both automatic classifiers and a human expert.|Here is another description: The diagnosis refers to the identification and classification of specific cardiac conditions based on electrocardiogram (ECG) readings. It is determined by certified cardiologists using standardized guidelines and presented software tools."},
{"diagnosis__should_be_reviewed_by__clinical_specialists_with_solid_experience_in_ecg_diagnosis": "The phrase \"should be reviewed by\" indicates a necessary step in the diagnostic process where an initial assessment or automated analysis is further examined and validated by qualified professionals. This review ensures accuracy and reliability in the diagnosis, especially in complex or borderline cases."},
{"clinical_specialists_with_solid_experience_in_ecg_diagnosis": "Clinical specialists with solid experience in ECG diagnosis are medical professionals, typically cardiologists or electrophysiologists, who have extensive training and practical experience in interpreting ECG results. Their expertise is crucial for confirming or refining diagnoses, particularly in challenging cases where automated systems may have limitations."},
