{"optimized_system_for_ecg_interpretation": "An optimized system for ECG interpretation refers to a sophisticated, automated approach to analyzing electrocardiogram data. This system aims to enhance the efficiency and accuracy of ECG diagnosis by leveraging advanced algorithms and machine learning techniques to interpret ECG results."},
{"optimized_system_for_ecg_interpretation__implies__cardiologists_would_only_be_needed_for_the_more_complex_cases": "The predicate \"implies\" in this context signifies a consequential relationship. It indicates that the implementation of an optimized system for ECG interpretation would lead to a specific outcome or condition, which is the reduced necessity for cardiologists in routine cases."},
{"cardiologists_would_only_be_needed_for_the_more_complex_cases": "The object \"cardiologists would only be needed for the more complex cases\" describes a scenario where the role of cardiologists is primarily reserved for handling intricate and challenging ECG interpretations. This suggests a shift in the workload, where routine and straightforward cases are managed by the automated system, leaving cardiologists to focus on cases that require their specialized expertise."},
