{"of_striking_utility_to_improve_access_to_health_care_in_low_and_middle_income_countries": "The object describes the potential impact of the system in low- and middle-income countries, where it could greatly improve access to healthcare, particularly in addressing the leading cause of death\u2014cardiovascular diseases\u2014in regions with inadequate systems of care for cardiac diseases."},
{"cardiovascular_diseases__are__the_leading_cause_of_death_in_low_and_middle_income_countries": "The phrase \"are the leading cause of\" signifies that cardiovascular diseases hold the primary position in terms of mortality rates within low- and middle-income countries. This predicate highlights the significant impact these diseases have on public health in these regions."},
{"the_leading_cause_of_death_in_low_and_middle_income_countries": "Low- and middle-income countries are nations that have a gross national income per capita below a certain threshold, as defined by the World Bank. These countries often face challenges in healthcare infrastructure, access to medical services, and resources for disease prevention and treatment."},
{"systems_of_care_for_cardiac_diseases": "Systems of care for cardiac diseases refer to the organized and coordinated healthcare services and resources dedicated to the prevention, diagnosis, treatment, and management of heart-related conditions. These systems encompass a range of medical professionals, facilities, and technologies aimed at addressing various cardiac diseases effectively."},
{"systems_of_care_for_cardiac_diseases__are__lacking_or_not_working_well_in_low_and_middle_income_countries": "The predicate \"are\" in this context signifies the current state or condition of the systems of care for cardiac diseases. It indicates that these systems, as they currently stand, face certain challenges or deficiencies."},
