{"ecg_recordings": "ECG recordings refer to the electrical activity of the heart captured over a specific period using electrocardiograph devices. These recordings are crucial for diagnosing various cardiac conditions and are typically analyzed by medical professionals.|Here is another description: ECG recordings refer to the digital capture of the electrical activity of the heart over a period of time using electrodes placed on the skin. These recordings are crucial for diagnosing various heart conditions and are typically performed in clinical settings using specialized equipment.|Here is another description: ECG recordings refer to the electrical signals captured from the heart's activity, which are crucial for diagnosing various cardiac conditions. These recordings are processed and analyzed to extract meaningful information about heart function.|Here is another description: ECG recordings refer to the electrical activity of the heart captured over a period, which are crucial for diagnosing various cardiac conditions. In this context, they are specifically formatted and preprocessed for input into a neural network.|Here is another description: ECG recordings are medical data collected from electrocardiograms, which record the electrical activity of the heart over a period of time using electrodes placed on the skin."},
{"ecg_recordings__duration__between_7_and_10_s": "The duration of the ECG recordings indicates the length of time over which the heart's electrical activity is captured. This duration is important as it determines the amount of data available for analysis and can impact the accuracy of the diagnosis."},
{"between_7_and_10_s": "The duration of between 7 and 10 seconds for ECG recordings means that the heart's electrical activity is monitored for a short period, which is standard for many diagnostic purposes. This timeframe allows for the capture of essential cardiac cycles while keeping the recording process efficient."},
{"ecg_recordings__sampled_at_frequencies__ranging_from_300_to_600_hz": "Sampled at frequencies indicates the rate at which the analog ECG signal is converted into a digital format. This process is essential for the storage, analysis, and transmission of ECG data, ensuring that the recorded signal accurately represents the heart's electrical activity."},
{"ranging_from_300_to_600_hz": "Ranging from 300 to 600 Hz describes the specific frequency range at which the ECG recordings are sampled. This range is chosen to capture the necessary details of the heart's electrical signals without introducing excessive noise or missing critical data points."},
{"specific_software": "The specific software is an in-house developed application utilized within the Telehealth Network of Minas Gerais (TNMG) system. It is designed to facilitate the handling of S12L-ECG exams in primary care facilities."},
{"specific_software__used_to__capture_the_ecg_tracings_upload_the_exam_with_patient_s_clinical_history_and_send_it_electronically_to_the_tnmg_analysis_center": "The predicate \"used to\" indicates the purpose and functionality of the specific software within the TNMG system. It highlights the actions that the software is designed to perform in relation to ECG exams."},
{"capture_the_ecg_tracings_upload_the_exam_with_patient_s_clinical_history_and_send_it_electronically_to_the_tnmg_analysis_center": "Capturing the ECG tracings, uploading the exam with the patient\u2019s clinical history, and sending it electronically to the TNMG analysis center are critical functions performed by the specific software. These actions ensure that the ECG data and associated clinical information are efficiently transmitted to cardiologists for analysis."},
{"cardiologist_from_tnmg": "The cardiologist from TNMG is a medical professional specializing in heart health, part of the experienced team within the Telehealth Network of Minas Gerais, a public telehealth system in Brazil."},
{"cardiologist_from_tnmg__analyzes__the_exam": "The predicate \"analyzes\" refers to the detailed examination and interpretation of medical data, in this case, the S12L-ECG exam, by the cardiologist to assess the patient's heart condition."},
{"the_exam": "The exam, specifically the S12L-ECG exam, is a medical test performed in primary care facilities using specialized equipment to record the electrical activity of the heart. It is then uploaded with the patient\u2019s clinical history and sent electronically to the TNMG analysis center for review."},
{"report": "The report is a document generated by a cardiologist after analyzing an S12L-ECG exam. It includes the findings and interpretations of the ECG tracings along with the patient\u2019s clinical history."},
{"report__is_generated_after__exam_analysis": "The phrase \"is generated after\" indicates the sequential relationship between the completion of the exam analysis and the creation of the report. It signifies that the report production is a subsequent step following the thorough examination and interpretation of the ECG data by the cardiologist."},
{"exam_analysis": "Exam analysis refers to the detailed evaluation of the S12L-ECG recordings by a cardiologist. This process involves interpreting the ECG tracings, assessing any abnormalities, and correlating the findings with the patient\u2019s clinical history to provide a comprehensive diagnostic insight."},
{"health_service": "The health service is an entity that provides medical care and services to individuals, including the capability to request and utilize specialized diagnostic tools and software for patient care."},
{"health_service__requested__exam": "The predicate'requested' indicates an action taken by the health service to formally ask for or demand a specific medical examination or procedure, in this case, an exam, to be conducted or provided."},
{"exam": "The exam refers to a specific medical test or procedure that is requested by the health service. In the context provided, it likely pertains to an electrocardiogram (ECG) analysis, which is a diagnostic tool used to assess the electrical activity of the heart.|Here is another description: The exam refers to a medical test, specifically an electrocardiogram (ECG), which is used to assess the electrical activity of the heart. This test is crucial for diagnosing various heart conditions and is part of the clinical information stored in a database for further analysis and epidemiological studies."},
{"exam__made_available_through__online_platform": "The phrase \"made available through\" indicates the method by which the exam results are distributed or accessed. In this context, it signifies that the results of the ECG exam are provided to healthcare professionals and possibly patients via a digital means, ensuring timely and efficient access to critical medical data."},
{"online_platform": "The online platform is a digital system or service that facilitates the storage, retrieval, and sharing of medical information, including ECG exam results. This platform is integral to the healthcare service, allowing for the integration of advanced ECG analysis software and the consolidation of clinical data for research and patient care."},
{"university_of_glasgow_ecg_analysis_program": "The University of Glasgow ECG analysis program is a software tool developed by the University of Glasgow for analyzing electrocardiogram (ECG) data. It automatically identifies various ECG waves, calculates axes, durations, amplitudes, and intervals, performs rhythm analysis, and provides diagnostic interpretations. The program has been integrated into in-house software and has been in use since December 2017."},
{"university_of_glasgow_ecg_analysis_program__incorporated_in__in_house_software": "The predicate 'incorporated in' signifies that the University of Glasgow ECG analysis program has been integrated into another system. This integration allows the program to function as a part of the larger system, enhancing its capabilities and providing additional features."},
{"in_house_software": "The in-house software refers to a custom-built application developed and maintained internally by an organization. In this context, it is the platform into which the University of Glasgow ECG analysis program has been incorporated, allowing for the automated analysis of ECGs and the storage of clinical information and cardiologist reports."},
{"university_of_glasgow_ecg_analysis_program__release__28_5": "The predicate'release' in this context refers to the version or iteration of the University of Glasgow ECG analysis program that was made available and integrated into the in-house software. This release signifies an update or new version of the software that includes improvements or new features."},
{"28_5": "The object '28.5' represents the specific version number of the University of Glasgow ECG analysis program that was released in January 2014. This version was incorporated into the in-house software since December 2017 and has been used for automatic ECG analysis and diagnostic interpretation."},
{"release_28_5": "Release 28.5 refers to a specific version of the University of Glasgow (Uni-G) ECG analysis program that was incorporated into the in-house software used for analyzing electrocardiograms."},
{"release_28_5__issued_in__january_2014": "The predicate \"issued in\" indicates the time frame during which the particular version of the software, release 28.5, was made available or released for use."},
{"january_2014": "January 2014 is the specific month and year when release 28.5 of the Uni-G ECG analysis program was issued, marking its availability for integration and use within the health service's software system."},
{"university_of_glasgow_ecg_analysis_program__used_since__december_2017": "The predicate \"used since\" indicates the start date from which the University of Glasgow ECG analysis program has been incorporated into the in-house software for ECG analysis within the health service."},
{"december_2017": "December 2017 is the specific month and year when the University of Glasgow ECG analysis program began to be used within the in-house software for ECG analysis, marking the integration of this tool into the health service's diagnostic processes."},
{"university_of_glasgow_ecg_analysis_program__used_to__automatically_identify_waves": "The predicate \"used to\" indicates the purpose or function of the University of Glasgow ECG analysis program. In this context, it signifies that the program is employed for the specific task of analyzing ECG data to identify various components and provide diagnostic information."},
{"automatically_identify_waves": "Automatically identifying waves refers to the capability of the University of Glasgow ECG analysis program to detect and label different waves present in an ECG tracing, such as P waves, QRS complexes, and T waves, without manual intervention. This function is crucial for accurate ECG interpretation and diagnosis."},
{"university_of_glasgow_ecg_analysis_program__used_to__calculate_axes_durations_amplitudes_and_intervals": "The predicate \"used to\" indicates the purpose or function of the University of Glasgow ECG analysis program. In this context, it describes how the program is employed to perform specific tasks related to ECG data analysis."},
{"calculate_axes_durations_amplitudes_and_intervals": "The objects \"calculate axes, durations, amplitudes and intervals\" refer to the specific measurements and parameters that the University of Glasgow ECG analysis program is designed to compute from ECG data. These parameters are crucial for diagnosing and interpreting heart conditions."},
{"university_of_glasgow_ecg_analysis_program__used_to__perform_rhythm_analysis": "The phrase \"used to\" indicates that the University of Glasgow ECG analysis program was employed for a specific purpose within the context of ECG data analysis. In this case, it was utilized to carry out a particular function related to ECG interpretation."},
{"perform_rhythm_analysis": "Performing rhythm analysis in the context of ECG data involves the automated examination of the electrical activity of the heart to determine the regularity and pattern of heartbeats. This analysis helps in identifying any abnormalities in heart rhythm, which is crucial for diagnosing various cardiac conditions."},
{"university_of_glasgow_ecg_analysis_program__used_to__give_diagnostic_interpretation": "The predicate \"used to\" indicates that the University of Glasgow ECG analysis program was employed for a specific purpose within the context of ECG data analysis. In this case, it was used to facilitate the process of diagnostic interpretation of ECG results."},
{"give_diagnostic_interpretation": "The object \"give diagnostic interpretation\" refers to the capability of the University of Glasgow ECG analysis program to provide automated diagnostic insights based on the analysis of ECG data. This feature assists healthcare professionals in making informed decisions regarding patient care."},
{"university_of_glasgow_ecg_analysis_program__provides__minnesota_codes": "The predicate 'provides' in this context indicates that the University of Glasgow ECG analysis program offers or supplies a specific feature or output, which in this case is the Minnesota codes. This means the software is capable of generating these codes as part of its analysis."},
{"minnesota_codes": "Minnesota codes are a standardized classification system used in electrocardiography to categorize ECG findings. They are particularly useful in epidemiological studies for consistent and comparable data analysis. The University of Glasgow ECG analysis program generates these codes as part of its diagnostic output.|Here is another description: Minnesota codes are a standardized classification system for electrocardiograms (ECGs), providing a systematic way to categorize and interpret ECG findings."},
{"minnesota_codes__used_in__epidemiological_studies": "The phrase \"used in\" indicates that Minnesota codes serve as a tool or method within a specific type of research or study."},
{"epidemiological_studies": "Epidemiological studies are research investigations that aim to understand the distribution and determinants of health-related states or events in specified populations, and the application of this study to the control of health problems."},
{"automatic_measurements": "Automatic measurements refer to the data and diagnostic interpretations generated by the University of Glasgow (Uni-G) ECG analysis program, which includes wave identification, calculation of axes, durations, amplitudes, intervals, rhythm analysis, and diagnostic interpretation.|Here is another description: Automatic measurements refer to the quantitative data and parameters derived from electrocardiograms (ECGs) without manual intervention. These measurements are crucial for the initial assessment and diagnosis of various cardiac conditions."},
{"automatic_measurements__shown_to__cardiologists": "The phrase \"shown to\" indicates the action of presenting or displaying the automatic measurements generated by the Uni-G ECG analysis program to the cardiologists for their review and inclusion in the medical report."},
{"cardiologists": "Cardiologists are medical doctors specialized in the diagnosis and treatment of heart-related conditions. In this context, they are the professionals responsible for reviewing the automatic measurements provided by the Uni-G ECG analysis program and incorporating them into the medical report.|Here is another description: Cardiologists are medical doctors who specialize in the diagnosis and treatment of heart and cardiovascular conditions. In this context, they are professionals who review and interpret the data provided by the University of Glasgow ECG analysis program to make clinical assessments.|Here is another description: Cardiologists are medical doctors who specialize in the diagnosis and treatment of heart-related conditions. In this context, they are certified professionals involved in annotating datasets for testing deep neural networks in electrocardiography."},
{"cardiologists__give__medical_report": "The act of 'giving' in this context refers to the process where cardiologists provide a formal document that includes their professional assessment and diagnosis based on the ECG data and automatic measurements provided by the analysis software."},
{"medical_report": "A medical report is a formal document prepared by healthcare professionals, in this case, cardiologists, that details the findings, diagnosis, and recommendations based on the patient's ECG and other relevant clinical data. This report is crucial for patient care and is stored in a database for future reference and study."},
{"clinical_information_digital_ecgs_tracings_cardiologist_report": "All clinical information, digital ECGs tracings, and the cardiologist report are essential components of patient health records. These elements provide comprehensive data on patient health status, diagnostic results, and professional medical assessments."},
{"clinical_information_digital_ecgs_tracings_cardiologist_report__stored_in__database": "The act of storing clinical information, digital ECGs tracings, and cardiologist reports in a database involves systematically organizing and preserving these critical health data for future reference, analysis, and retrieval."},
{"database": "The database serves as a centralized repository for storing various types of clinical data, including patient information, ECG tracings, and medical reports. It ensures data integrity, accessibility, and security for use in clinical and epidemiological studies."},
{"previously_stored_data": "Previously stored data refers to the clinical information, digital ECG tracings, and cardiologist reports that were saved in the database prior to the integration of the Uni-G software. This data encompasses a wide range of patient records and diagnostic information accumulated over time."},
{"previously_stored_data__analyzed_by__uni_g_software": "Analyzed by signifies the process where the previously stored data underwent examination and interpretation using the Uni-G software. This predicate highlights the action taken to ensure that all historical data was processed and standardized with the new software\u2019s capabilities."},
{"uni_g_software": "Uni-G software is an ECG analysis program developed by the University of Glasgow, utilized for automatically identifying waves, calculating axes, durations, amplitudes, and intervals, performing rhythm analysis, and providing diagnostic interpretations and Minnesota codes. It has been integrated into the in-house software to enhance the analysis of ECG data."},
{"code_study__established_to__standardize_and_consolidate_database": "The phrase \"established to\" indicates the purpose or goal for which the CODE study was created. It signifies that the study was set up with a specific objective in mind, which in this case is to enhance the database used for clinical and epidemiological research."},
{"standardize_and_consolidate_database": "The objective to \"standardize and consolidate database\" refers to the process of organizing and unifying the data within the database to ensure consistency, accuracy, and ease of access. This involves setting uniform standards for data entry, storage, and retrieval, as well as merging disparate data sets into a coherent whole."},
{"code_study__for__clinical_and_epidemiological_studies": "The predicate \"for\" in this context signifies the purpose or intended use of the CODE study. It indicates that the study was designed and implemented with a specific goal in mind, which is to support certain types of research."},
{"clinical_and_epidemiological_studies": "Clinical and epidemiological studies are research efforts that aim to understand the distribution, determinants, and effects of health and diseases in specified populations. These studies often rely on large datasets to draw meaningful conclusions about health trends and outcomes."},
{"data_for_patients_above_16_years_old": "The data refers to clinical information, digital ECG tracings, and cardiologist reports for patients above 16 years old, which were stored in a database and analyzed using the University of Glasgow ECG analysis program."},
{"data_for_patients_above_16_years_old__obtained_between__2010_and_2016": "The predicate \"obtained between\" indicates the time frame during which the data for patients above 16 years old was collected and stored in the database."},
{"2010_and_2016": "The time frame of 2010 and 2016 represents the period during which the data for patients above 16 years old was gathered, analyzed, and incorporated into the database for clinical and epidemiological studies."},
{"data": "The data refers to clinical information, digital ECG tracings, and cardiologist reports stored in a database, specifically for patients above 16 years old, collected between 2010 and 2016 as part of the CODE study.|Here is another description: The data refers to information collected and analyzed within the context of the CODE study, specifically focusing on patients above 16 years old. This data encompasses clinical information, digital ECG tracings, and cardiologist reports, all stored in a dedicated database.|Here is another description: The data refers to the information collected from patients above 16 years old, obtained between 2010 and 2016, and includes clinical information, digital ECG tracings, and cardiologist reports.|Here is another description: The subject 'data' refers to the information or facts that are being discussed in the context, specifically the source data underlying Supplementary Figs. 1 and 2."},
{"data__used_in__training_and_validation_set": "The phrase \"used in\" indicates the application or utilization of the data within a specific process or set, in this case, for the purposes of machine learning model development."},
{"training_and_validation_set": "The training and validation set are subsets of data used in machine learning to train a model (training set) and to fine-tune model parameters and evaluate its performance (validation set) before final testing."},
{"data__used_from__april_to_september_2018": "The phrase \"used from\" indicates the specific time period during which the data was utilized for a particular purpose within the study, highlighting its application in the test set phase of the research."},
{"april_to_september_2018": "The period from April to September 2018 signifies a defined timeframe within the study where the data was specifically employed. This period is crucial as it represents the test set phase, where the data was used to evaluate the effectiveness and accuracy of the Uni-G ECG analysis program in a real-world clinical setting."},
{"data__used_in__test_set": "The phrase \"used in\" indicates that the data was utilized as part of a process or system, specifically within the context of the study's methodology for evaluating or testing a certain aspect, such as the performance of software or a diagnostic tool."},
{"test_set": "The test set is a subset of data reserved for evaluating the final model or system after it has been trained and validated. It is used to assess the generalization capability of the model on unseen data."},
{"text_report": "A text report is a document containing a textual description of abnormalities observed in a medical exam, specifically used in this context for cardiology assessments."},
{"text_report__is_used_for__labeling_training_data": "The phrase \"is used for\" indicates the purpose or function of the text report in the process of labeling training data, highlighting its role in the classification and analysis of medical information."},
{"labeling_training_data": "Labeling training data refers to the process of assigning specific medical labels or diagnoses to textual descriptions extracted from medical reports, which are then used to train and validate machine learning models for medical classification tasks."},
{"cardiologist_report": "The cardiologist report is a document generated by a cardiologist after examining a patient's medical data, specifically focusing on cardiac-related issues."},
{"cardiologist_report__is_available_as__textual_description_of_abnormalities": "The phrase \"is available as\" indicates the format or manner in which the cardiologist report is presented or can be accessed, in this case, as a textual description."},
{"textual_description_of_abnormalities": "The textual description of abnormalities refers to a written account detailing any deviations from normal cardiac function or structure that are identified during the examination."},
{"label": "The label refers to a classification or category assigned to a medical condition based on the analysis of textual data. In this context, it represents the specific medical diagnosis extracted from the textual report.|Here is another description: The label refers to the ECG diagnosis chosen by the specialist among a number of prespecified classes of abnormalities, as codified directly into the classes used in the study."},
{"label__is_extracted_from__textual_report": "The predicate \"is extracted from\" indicates the process by which the label is derived. It involves analyzing and processing the textual report to identify and classify the medical condition described within it."},
{"textual_report": "The textual report is a written document created by a cardiologist that describes the abnormalities observed in a medical exam. It serves as the source from which the label is extracted using a series of computational steps including preprocessing, application of a classification algorithm, and rule-based disambiguation."},
{"text": "The text refers to the textual description of abnormalities in a cardiologist's report, which is used for labeling training data in a medical classification task."},
{"text__is_preprocessed_by__removing_stop_words_and_generating_ngrams": "The text is preprocessed by removing stop-words and generating ngrams, which is a necessary step in preparing the text data for further analysis and classification by the Lazy Associative Classifier (LAC)."},
{"removing_stop_words_and_generating_ngrams": "Removing stop-words and generating ngrams involves eliminating common, non-informative words from the text and creating combinations of words (ngrams) that are more meaningful for the classification task. This preprocessing step helps in improving the accuracy and efficiency of the subsequent classification process."},
{"lazy_associative_classifier_lac": "The Lazy Associative Classifier (LAC) is a machine learning model designed to classify text data by associating n-grams with labels. It operates by leveraging preprocessed text data to generate meaningful classifications."},
{"lazy_associative_classifier_lac__is_trained_on__2800_sample_dictionary_from_real_diagnoses_text_reports": "The phrase \"is trained on\" indicates that the Lazy Associative Classifier (LAC) has undergone a training process using a specific dataset. This training enables the classifier to learn patterns and associations within the data, which it then applies to new, unseen text data for classification purposes."},
{"2800_sample_dictionary_from_real_diagnoses_text_reports": "The 2800-sample dictionary from real diagnoses text reports is a dataset used to train the Lazy Associative Classifier (LAC). This dictionary consists of 2800 samples of textual diagnoses, which provide the classifier with the necessary context and patterns to accurately label new medical reports."},
{"lac": "The Lazy Associative Classifier (LAC) is a machine learning model used for classification tasks. It is trained on a dictionary of 2800 samples derived from real diagnoses text reports."},
{"lac__is_applied_to__n_grams": "The phrase \"is applied to\" indicates the action of using the LAC model on a specific dataset or input, in this case, n-grams extracted from medical reports."},
{"n_grams": "N-grams are contiguous sequences of n items from a given sample of text or speech. In this context, they are generated from medical reports after preprocessing, which involves removing stop-words."},
{"text_label": "The text label refers to the extracted label from a textual report, specifically a cardiologist's report describing abnormalities in a medical exam. This label is derived through a systematic process involving text preprocessing and classification."},
{"text_label__is_obtained_using__lac_result_in_a_rule_based_classifier_for_class_disambiguation": "The phrase \"is obtained using\" indicates the method or process by which the text label is derived. In this context, it specifies that the text label is generated through the application of a particular classification technique following text preprocessing."},
{"lac_result_in_a_rule_based_classifier_for_class_disambiguation": "The LAC result in a rule-based classifier for class disambiguation is a method used to determine the text label. It involves applying the Lazy Associative Classifier (LAC) to n-grams from the medical report and then using a rule-based classifier to disambiguate the class, ensuring accurate labeling of the medical data."},
{"classification_model": "The classification model is a system designed to categorize medical reports into predefined classes based on textual descriptions of abnormalities. It utilizes a combination of preprocessing, a Lazy Associative Classifier, and a rule-based classifier for accurate label extraction."},
{"classification_model__was_tested_on__4557_medical_reports": "The phrase \"was tested on\" indicates that the classification model underwent evaluation using a specific dataset to assess its performance and accuracy in labeling medical reports."},
{"4557_medical_reports": "The 4557 medical reports are a collection of textual descriptions of medical examinations, manually labeled by a certified cardiologist. These reports were used as a test dataset to evaluate the classification model's ability to accurately identify and categorize medical conditions."},
{"medical_reports": "Medical reports are detailed documents that describe the findings and diagnoses from medical examinations, often containing textual descriptions of abnormalities."},
{"medical_reports__were_labeled_by__certified_cardiologist": "The act of labeling involves categorizing or tagging the medical reports based on the described abnormalities and diagnoses, which is a critical step in preparing data for machine learning models."},
{"certified_cardiologist": "A certified cardiologist is a medical professional who has specialized training and certification in diagnosing and treating heart conditions, and in this context, they are responsible for accurately labeling the medical reports.|Here is another description: A certified cardiologist with experience in ECG interpretation, responsible for overseeing the medical students during their manual review of ECGs to ensure accuracy and quality in the diagnostic process.|Here is another description: A certified cardiologist is a medical professional who has completed specialized training and certification in the field of cardiology, focusing on the diagnosis and treatment of heart-related conditions."},
{"cardiologist__was_presented_with__free_text": "The phrase \"was presented with\" indicates that the cardiologist was given or shown something\u2014in this case, free-text medical reports\u2014as part of their task to label these reports according to prespecified classes."},
{"free_text": "The free-text refers to the unstructured, textual descriptions of abnormalities found in medical exams, which the cardiologist uses to assign labels. These texts are part of the medical reports that have not been formatted into a structured data set and require interpretation by the cardiologist."},
{"cardiologist__was_required_to_choose_among__prespecified_classes": "The cardiologist was required to choose among indicates a process where the cardiologist had to select the most appropriate diagnosis from a set of predefined categories based on the textual description provided in the medical report."},
{"prespecified_classes": "The prespecified classes refer to a set of predefined diagnostic categories that the cardiologist must choose from when labeling the medical reports. These classes include specific heart conditions such as 1st degree Atrioventricular block (1dAVb), Right Bundle Branch Block (RBBB), Left Bundle Branch Block (LBBB), Sinus Bradycardia (SB), Atrial Fibrillation (AF), and ST-segment changes (ST)."},
{"classification_step": "The classification step refers to a specific stage in a three-step procedure used to extract labels from textual medical reports. This step involves applying a trained classifier to preprocessed text to determine the correct medical label."},
{"classification_step__recovered__true_medical_label_with_good_results": "The predicate \"recovered\" in this context means that the classification step was successful in identifying and retrieving the correct medical label from the textual description provided in the cardiologist's report."},
{"true_medical_label_with_good_results": "The true medical label with good results signifies the accurate and correct medical diagnosis that was successfully identified by the classification step. The good results are indicated by high macro F1 scores for various medical conditions."},
{"macro_f1_score": "The macro F1 score is a metric for evaluating classification models with multiple classes, providing a balanced measure of accuracy by considering both precision and recall, especially useful in scenarios with imbalanced datasets."},
{"macro_f1_score__achieved__0_729_for_1davb": "The predicate 'achieved' indicates that the macro F1 score was obtained or reached as a result of applying the classification model to the medical reports. This score reflects the model's performance in accurately identifying and categorizing the medical conditions described in the text reports."},
{"0_729_for_1davb": "The object '0.729 for 1dAVb' specifies the macro F1 score obtained for the class 1dAVb, which is one of the prespecified classes in the medical reports. This score represents the model's ability to correctly classify instances of 1dAVb among the other classes, with a value of 0.729 indicating a moderate level of performance for this particular class."},
{"macro_f1_score__achieved__0_849_for_rbbb": "The predicate 'achieved' indicates that the macro F1 score was obtained or reached as a result of applying the classification model to the medical reports. This score reflects the model's effectiveness in correctly identifying and categorizing the abnormalities described in the textual reports."},
{"0_849_for_rbbb": "The object '0.849 for RBBB' specifies the macro F1 score obtained for the class Right Bundle Branch Block (RBBB). This score of 0.849 suggests a high level of accuracy in the model's ability to correctly classify instances of RBBB from the textual descriptions provided in the medical reports."},
{"macro_f1_score__achieved__0_838_for_lbbb": "The predicate 'achieved' indicates that the macro F1 score was obtained or reached as a result of applying the classification model to the medical reports. This score reflects the model's performance in correctly identifying and categorizing the medical labels from the text reports."},
{"0_838_for_lbbb": "The object '0.838 for LBBB' specifies the macro F1 score obtained for the class Left Bundle Branch Block (LBBB). This score of 0.838 suggests a relatively high level of accuracy and reliability in the model's ability to classify LBBB from the textual descriptions provided in the medical reports."},
{"macro_f1_score__achieved__0_991_for_sb": "The predicate 'achieved' indicates that the macro F1 score was obtained or reached as a result of applying the classification model to the medical reports. This score reflects the model's effectiveness in correctly identifying the specified classes from the textual descriptions."},
{"0_991_for_sb": "The object '0.991 for SB' represents the specific macro F1 score achieved for the class Sinus Bradycardia (SB) in the classification task. This high score suggests that the model performed exceptionally well in identifying instances of Sinus Bradycardia from the textual reports."},
{"macro_f1_score__achieved__0_993_for_af": "The predicate 'achieved' indicates that the macro F1 score was obtained or reached as a result of applying the classification model to the medical reports. This score reflects the model's performance in accurately classifying the medical conditions described in the text reports."},
{"0_993_for_af": "The object '0.993 for AF' represents the specific macro F1 score achieved for the class 'Atrial Fibrillation' (AF). This high score suggests that the classification model performed exceptionally well in identifying and categorizing instances of Atrial Fibrillation within the medical reports."},
{"macro_f1_score__achieved__0_974_for_st": "The predicate 'achieved' indicates that the macro F1 score was obtained or reached as a result of applying the classification model to the medical reports. This score reflects the model's effectiveness in correctly identifying the specified classes from the textual descriptions."},
{"0_974_for_st": "The object '0.974 for ST' represents the specific macro F1 score obtained for the class labeled as ST (sinus tachycardia) in the classification of medical reports. This high score suggests that the model performed exceptionally well in identifying this particular class from the textual data."},
{"training_and_validation_datasets": "The training and validation datasets are collections of data used to train and validate machine learning models, ensuring they perform accurately and reliably on unseen data.|Here is another description: The training and validation datasets are collections of data used for machine learning model training and performance evaluation, respectively. These datasets require accurate annotation to ensure the model learns correctly and can be effectively assessed.|Here is another description: The training and validation datasets are collections of data used to train and validate machine learning models, ensuring they can accurately perform tasks such as classification or prediction."},
{"training_and_validation_datasets__were_annotated_using__uni_g_statements_and_minnesota_codes": "The phrase \"were annotated using\" indicates the process by which the datasets were labeled or marked up with specific information to enhance their utility for training and validation purposes."},
{"uni_g_statements_and_minnesota_codes": "Uni-G statements and Minnesota codes are standardized diagnostic criteria and codes used in the field of cardiology to describe and classify electrocardiogram (ECG) findings, aiding in the consistent interpretation and analysis of cardiac data.|Here is another description: The Uni-G statements and Minnesota codes are specific annotations and classifications used in medical datasets, particularly for cardiovascular research. They provide structured information that can be utilized for training and validating machine learning models."},
