{"use_the_convolutional_architecture_known_as_vgg": "The convolutional architecture known as VGG is a specific type of neural network architecture that was experimented with as part of the procedure. VGG, named after the Visual Geometry Group at the University of Oxford, is renowned for its deep convolutional neural networks, which have been successful in various computer vision tasks."},
{"procedure__also_tried_to__switch_the_order_of_activation_and_batch_normalization_layer": "\"Also tried to\" indicates an experimental approach where additional modifications or alternative configurations were attempted as part of the procedure to enhance the performance or effectiveness of the machine learning model."},
