{"this_research__was_supported_by__brazilian_agencies_cnpq_capes_and_fapemig": "The phrase \"was supported by\" indicates that the research received financial or resource-based assistance from certain entities, enabling its progression and completion."},
{"brazilian_agencies_cnpq_capes_and_fapemig": "Brazilian Agencies CNPq, CAPES, and FAPEMIG are governmental and educational funding bodies in Brazil that provide financial support to research projects, scholars, and educational programs to foster scientific and technological development in the country."},
{"this_research__was_supported_by__projects_iats_masweb_inct_cyber_rede_de_teleassist\u00eancia_de_minas_gerais_and_atmosphere": "The phrase \"was supported by\" indicates the relationship where the research received financial or resource-based assistance from various projects and agencies."},
{"projects_iats_masweb_inct_cyber_rede_de_teleassist\u00eancia_de_minas_gerais_and_atmosphere": "Projects IATS, MASWeb, INCT-Cyber, Rede de Teleassist\u00eancia de Minas Gerais, and Atmosphere are specific initiatives or programs that provided support or funding to the research. These projects are likely related to technology, innovation, or scientific research, given their names and the context of the acknowledgments."},
{"this_research__was_supported_by__wallenberg_ai_autonomous_systems_and_software_program_wasp_funded_by_knut_and_alice_wallenberg_foundation": "The phrase \"was supported by\" indicates a financial or resource-based backing provided to the research. This support is crucial for the execution and completion of the research, enabling the researchers to access necessary funds, equipment, and other resources."},
{"wallenberg_ai_autonomous_systems_and_software_program_wasp_funded_by_knut_and_alice_wallenberg_foundation": "The Wallenberg AI, Autonomous Systems and Software Program (WASP) is a funding initiative backed by the Knut and Alice Wallenberg Foundation. This program aims to support research and development in the fields of artificial intelligence, autonomous systems, and software, fostering innovation and advancement in these areas."},
{"we__thank__nvidia_for_awarding_our_project_with_a_titan_v_gpu": "The predicate \"thank\" indicates an expression of gratitude or acknowledgment from the subject towards the object. In this context, it signifies the researchers' appreciation for the support and resources provided by the object, which has contributed to the success of their project."},
{"nvidia_for_awarding_our_project_with_a_titan_v_gpu": "The object \"NVIDIA for awarding our project with a Titan V GPU\" refers to the technology company NVIDIA, which has supported the researchers' project by providing a high-performance Titan V GPU. This award is acknowledged as a significant contribution to the project's capabilities and outcomes."},
{"a_l_p_r": "A.L.P.R. is an individual or entity involved in research activities, as indicated by the receipt of scholarships aimed at supporting research efforts.|Here is another description: A.L.P.R is an individual who played a key role in the project by being responsible for the study design and acting as the project leader. Their contributions were critical in steering the project towards its goals.|Here is another description: A.L.P.R is an individual who played a key role in the study by contributing to the study design and conceiving the project. They were instrumental in the overall direction and planning of the research.|Here is another description: A.L.P.R. is one of the designated recipients for correspondence and requests for materials, alongside A.H.R. and T.B.S\u00f6n., implying a role or responsibility in managing or providing the requested materials or information."},
{"a_l_p_r__receives__unrestricted_research_scholarships_from_cnpq_and_fapemig_ppm": "The predicate \"receives\" indicates the action of being granted or awarded something, in this case, financial support in the form of scholarships to facilitate research activities."},
{"unrestricted_research_scholarships_from_cnpq_and_fapemig_ppm": "Unrestricted research scholarships from CNPq and FAPEMIG (PPM) are financial awards provided by the Brazilian National Council for Scientific and Technological Development (CNPq) and the Research Foundation of the State of Minas Gerais (FAPEMIG) under the PPM program, intended to support research without specific restrictions on the research topic."},
{"w_m_jr": "W.M.Jr. is an individual acknowledged for receiving financial support for research activities. They are part of a group of researchers who have been awarded various scholarships and funding from multiple agencies to support their projects."},
{"w_m_jr__receives__an_unrestricted_research_scholarship_from_cnpq": "The predicate \"receives\" indicates the action of being granted or awarded something, in this case, a scholarship. It signifies the transfer of financial support from a funding agency to a researcher to aid in their research endeavors."},
{"an_unrestricted_research_scholarship_from_cnpq": "An unrestricted research scholarship from CNPq is a form of financial aid provided by the Brazilian National Council for Scientific and Technological Development (CNPq) to support research activities without specific restrictions on how the funds can be used. This type of scholarship allows researchers the flexibility to allocate resources as needed for their projects."},
{"a_h_r": "A.H.R. is an individual acknowledged for receiving financial support for research activities. Their involvement in the research is supported by scholarships, which are detailed in the acknowledgments section of a research document.|Here is another description: A.H.R. is one of the contributors to the study, involved in various aspects including the implementation and tuning of the deep neural network, and significantly, the statistical analysis of the test data.|Here is another description: A.H.R. is one of the authors involved in the study, specifically responsible for the statistical analysis of the test data and the creation of visual representations of the data.|Here is another description: A.H.R. is one of the designated individuals or entities to whom correspondence and requests for materials should be directed, suggesting a role in managing or providing the requested resources."},
{"a_h_r__receives__scholarships_from_capes_and_cnpq": "The predicate \"receives\" indicates the action of being granted or awarded something, in this case, financial support in the form of scholarships. It signifies the transfer of resources from funding agencies to the individual to support their research endeavors."},
{"scholarships_from_capes_and_cnpq": "The object \"scholarships from CAPES and CNPq\" refers to financial awards provided by two Brazilian funding agencies: CAPES (Coordination for the Improvement of Higher Education Personnel) and CNPq (National Council for Scientific and Technological Development). These scholarships are intended to support research activities and are unrestricted, meaning they can be used for a wide range of research-related expenses."},
{"m_h_r_and_d_m_o": "M.H.R. and D.M.O. are individuals who are part of a research project supported by multiple funding agencies and institutions. Their work is acknowledged in the context of receiving various scholarships and support for their research endeavors."},
{"m_h_r_and_d_m_o__receive__google_latin_america_research_award_scholarships": "The predicate \"receive\" indicates that M.H.R. and D.M.O. have been granted or awarded something, specifically in the form of scholarships, as part of their research support."},
{"google_latin_america_research_award_scholarships": "The Google Latin America Research Award scholarships are financial awards provided by Google to support research projects in Latin America. These scholarships are part of the acknowledgments for the research project, highlighting external funding and recognition."},
{"none_of_the_funding_agencies": "The subject refers to the funding agencies that supported the research, including Brazilian Agencies CNPq, CAPES, and FAPEMIG, projects IATS, MASWeb, INCT-Cyber, Rede de Teleassist\u00eancia de Minas Gerais and Atmosphere, the Wallenberg AI, Autonomous Systems and Software Program (WASP) funded by Knut and Alice Wallenberg Foundation, NVIDIA, and scholarship providers CNPq, FAPEMIG, CAPES, and Google Latin America Research Award."},
{"none_of_the_funding_agencies__had_any_role_in__the_design_analysis_or_interpretation_of_the_study": "The predicate indicates that the funding agencies did not have any involvement or influence in certain aspects of the research process."},
{"the_design_analysis_or_interpretation_of_the_study": "The object describes the specific aspects of the study that the funding agencies did not influence, which include the design, analysis, or interpretation of the study."},
{"open_access_funding": "Open access funding refers to financial support provided to make research publications freely available to readers. This funding ensures that the research is accessible to a wider audience without paywalls or subscription barriers."},
{"open_access_funding__provided_by__uppsala_university": "The predicate \"provided by\" indicates the source or entity responsible for offering the open access funding. It establishes a relationship where Uppsala University is the provider of the funding that enables the research to be openly accessible."},
{"a_h_r_m_h_r_g_m_m_p_d_m_o_p_r_g_j_a_c_m_p_s_f_and_a_l_p_r": "A.H.R., M.H.R., G.M.M.P., D.M.O., P.R.G., J.A.C, M.P.S.F, and A.L.P.R. are a group of authors who contributed to various aspects of a research project, including study design, data preprocessing, implementation of methodologies, and writing the manuscript."},
{"a_h_r_m_h_r_g_m_m_p_d_m_o_p_r_g_j_a_c_m_p_s_f_and_a_l_p_r__were_responsible_for__the_study_design": "The phrase \"were responsible for\" indicates that the subjects played a key role in the creation and execution of the study design, suggesting they had significant input and decision-making authority in shaping the research framework."},
{"the_study_design": "The study design refers to the overall plan and structure of the research project, including the methodology, data collection processes, and analytical approaches that were employed to achieve the research objectives."},
{"a_l_p_r__conceived__the_project": "The term 'conceived' in this context refers to the act of originating or bringing into existence the project. It highlights the initial idea and planning phase that A.L.P.R was instrumental in initiating."},
{"the_project": "The project in question is a collaborative effort involving multiple authors who contributed to various aspects such as study design, implementation of methodologies, data analysis, and manuscript writing. The project's success relied on the combined efforts and expertise of all involved parties."},
{"a_l_p_r__acted_as__project_leader": "The predicate \"acted as\" signifies the role or function that A.L.P.R performed within the project. It indicates that A.L.P.R took on a specific responsibility or position to facilitate the project's progress and success."},
{"project_leader": "The object \"project leader\" refers to the role A.L.P.R assumed in the project, which involved overseeing and guiding the project's execution. As the project leader, A.L.P.R would have been responsible for coordinating efforts, making critical decisions, and ensuring that the project stayed on track towards its objectives."},
{"a_h_r_m_h_r_and_c_r_a": "A.H.R., M.H.R, and C.R.A. are individuals involved in the study who contributed to the design and implementation of the deep neural network. They played a key role in the technical aspects of the project.|Here is another description: A.H.R., M.H.R, and C.R.A. are individuals who contributed to the technical aspects of a research project involving a deep neural network. They were involved in the selection of the network's architecture."},
{"a_h_r_m_h_r_and_c_r_a__chose__the_architecture": "The predicate \"chose\" indicates the action taken by A.H.R., M.H.R, and C.R.A. in selecting a specific design or structure for the deep neural network, which is critical for the performance and functionality of the model."},
{"the_architecture": "The architecture refers to the specific design and structure of the deep neural network that was selected by A.H.R., M.H.R, and C.R.A. This choice is fundamental as it determines how the neural network processes information and learns from the data."},
{"a_h_r_m_h_r_and_c_r_a__implemented_and_tuned__the_deep_neural_network": "The phrase \"implemented and tuned\" refers to the actions taken by the subjects to bring the deep neural network into functional existence and to optimize its performance. This involves coding the network according to the chosen architecture and adjusting its parameters to improve accuracy and efficiency."},
{"the_deep_neural_network": "The deep neural network is a complex machine learning model characterized by multiple layers that enable it to learn and make decisions based on data. In this context, it is the central technological component of the research project that the subjects worked on."},
{"a_h_r__did__the_statistical_analysis_of_the_test_data": "The predicate \"did\" indicates that A.H.R. was actively involved in performing the statistical analysis of the test data as part of their contributions to the study."},
{"the_statistical_analysis_of_the_test_data": "The statistical analysis of the test data refers to the process of examining and interpreting the data collected from tests to draw conclusions, identify patterns, and validate the effectiveness of the implemented methodologies in the study."},
{"a_h_r__generated__the_figures_and_tables": "The term 'generated' in this context refers to the action of creating or producing something, in this case, figures and tables, as part of the statistical analysis of the test data."},
{"the_figures_and_tables": "The figures and tables are visual representations of the data that were produced as part of the statistical analysis. They are essential components of the study, providing a clear and concise way to present the results and findings."},
{"m_h_r_g_m_m_p_j_a_c": "M.H.R., G.M.M.P, and J.A.C. are individuals who contributed to a research project involving the development and application of a deep neural network. Their roles included specific tasks related to data preparation."},
{"m_h_r_g_m_m_p_j_a_c__were_responsible_for__the_preprocessing_and_annotating_the_datasets": "The phrase \"were responsible for\" indicates that M.H.R., G.M.M.P, and J.A.C. had the duty or obligation to carry out certain tasks within the research project. This predicate signifies their specific contributions to the project."},
{"the_preprocessing_and_annotating_the_datasets": "The preprocessing and annotating of the datasets refer to the initial steps taken to prepare the data for use in the deep neural network. Preprocessing involves cleaning and transforming the raw data into a suitable format, while annotating means labeling the data to provide context or meaning for the neural network to learn from."},
{"g_m_m_p": "G.M.M.P is one of the contributors to the study, involved in various stages of the project including preprocessing, annotating datasets, and specifically tasked with error analysis."},
{"g_m_m_p__was_responsible_for__the_error_analysis": "The phrase \"was responsible for\" indicates a direct involvement and accountability of G.M.M.P in conducting the error analysis as part of their contributions to the study."},
{"d_m_o": "D.M.O. is one of the contributors to a research project involving the design and implementation of a deep neural network system. They played a specific role in the development process."},
{"d_m_o__implemented__the_semi_supervised_methodology_to_extract_the_text_label": "The action 'implemented' refers to the execution and realization of a planned methodology or system. In this context, it signifies that D.M.O. carried out the development of a specific technique as part of the project."},
{"the_semi_supervised_methodology_to_extract_the_text_label": "The semi-supervised methodology to extract the text label is a technique developed as part of a research project. It involves using both labeled and unlabeled data to train a model that can extract text labels, likely for annotating datasets or similar tasks."},
{"p_r_g": "P.R.G. is one of the contributors to the study, involved in various aspects of the project including the implementation of specific components."},
{"p_r_g__implemented__the_user_interface_used_to_generate_the_dataset": "The predicate \"implemented\" indicates that P.R.G. was responsible for the creation and execution of a particular part of the project, specifically the user interface."},
{"the_user_interface_used_to_generate_the_dataset": "The user interface used to generate the dataset is a tool developed to facilitate the creation and management of the dataset utilized in the study. It was specifically implemented by P.R.G. as part of his contributions to the project."},
{"p_r_g_and_m_p_s_f": "P.R.G. and M.P.S.F. are individuals who contributed to a research project involving the development and management of a database. Their roles were specific to the technical aspects of database handling within the project."},
{"p_r_g_and_m_p_s_f__were_responsible_for__maintenance_and_extraction_of_the_database": "The phrase \"were responsible for\" indicates a duty or role assigned to P.R.G. and M.P.S.F. in the context of the research project. It signifies that they had the task of ensuring the proper functioning and upkeep of the database, as well as extracting data from it as needed for the project's objectives."},
{"maintenance_and_extraction_of_the_database": "The maintenance and extraction of the database refer to the ongoing processes required to keep the database operational and to retrieve data from it. Maintenance would involve updating, securing, and troubleshooting the database, while extraction would involve querying the database to obtain specific data for analysis or use in the project."},
{"p_w_m_w_m_jr_and_t_b_s": "P.W.M., W.M.Jr., and T.B.S. are individuals who contributed to the study by providing their expertise and insights."},
{"p_w_m_w_m_jr_and_t_b_s__helped_in__the_interpretation_of_the_data": "The phrase \"helped in\" indicates that these individuals provided assistance or support in a specific task or process related to the study."},
{"the_interpretation_of_the_data": "The interpretation of the data refers to the process of analyzing and making sense of the information collected during the study, which is a critical step in drawing conclusions and making informed decisions."},
{"a_h_r_m_h_r_p_w_m_t_b_s_and_a_l_p_r": "A.H.R., M.H.R, P.W.M., T.B.S. and A.L.P.R. are individuals who were part of a collaborative research project. They played various roles in the study, including study design, project leadership, implementation of methodologies, data analysis, and database management."},
{"a_h_r_m_h_r_p_w_m_t_b_s_and_a_l_p_r__contributed_to__the_writing": "The phrase \"contributed to\" indicates that the individuals listed as the subject of the triple played a role in the creation or development of something. In this context, it specifically refers to their involvement in the writing process of a manuscript."},
{"the_writing": "The writing refers to the process of composing and drafting a manuscript that documents the research conducted by the team. This manuscript includes details about the study design, methodologies used, data analysis, and the interpretation of results."},
{"all_authors": "All authors refer to the collective group of individuals who have contributed to the creation and development of the manuscript. This includes those involved in study design, data analysis, implementation of methodologies, and other critical roles necessary for the completion of the research project.|Here is another description: All authors refers to the collective group of individuals who have contributed to the research project and manuscript. This includes those involved in study design, data collection, analysis, and writing."},
{"all_authors__revised__it_critically_for_important_intellectual_content": "The predicate \"revised\" indicates that the subject, in this case, all authors, have critically reviewed and made necessary changes to the manuscript. This process involves assessing the intellectual content to ensure accuracy, clarity, and relevance, thereby enhancing the overall quality of the work."},
{"it_critically_for_important_intellectual_content": "\"It critically for important intellectual content\" refers to the thorough and thoughtful examination of the manuscript\u2019s core ideas, arguments, and data. This object highlights the significance of ensuring that the intellectual contributions within the manuscript are sound, well-supported, and effectively communicated to the readers."},
{"all_authors__read_and_approved__the_submitted_manuscript": "Read and approved signifies that each author has thoroughly reviewed the manuscript, ensuring its accuracy, relevance, and adherence to scientific standards before submission. This process is crucial for maintaining the integrity and quality of the research."},
{"the_submitted_manuscript": "The submitted manuscript is the final document prepared by the authors for publication, encapsulating the research findings, methodology, results, and conclusions of the study. It represents the culmination of the authors' collaborative efforts."},
{"this_study": "This study refers to a research project that involves the secondary analysis of anonymized data stored in the TNMG (presumably a database or repository). The study has undergone ethical review and has been sanctioned by a recognized ethics committee.|Here is another description: This study refers to a research project that involves a secondary analysis of anonymized data stored in the TNMG. It is designed to comply with all relevant ethical regulations."},
{"this_study__complies_with__all_relevant_ethical_regulations": "The phrase \"complies with\" indicates that the study adheres to and follows the guidelines, standards, and legal requirements set forth by relevant authorities. In this context, it means the study has been conducted in accordance with ethical regulations."},
{"all_relevant_ethical_regulations": "All relevant ethical regulations encompass the rules, guidelines, and legal requirements established to ensure the ethical conduct of research. These regulations are designed to protect the rights, safety, and well-being of participants and to maintain the integrity of the research process."},
{"this_study__was_approved_by__the_research_ethics_committee_of_the_universidade_federal_de_minas_gerais": "The phrase \"was approved by\" indicates that the study underwent a review process and received formal authorization from a designated body to proceed with its research activities."},
{"the_research_ethics_committee_of_the_universidade_federal_de_minas_gerais": "The Research Ethics Committee of the Universidade Federal de Minas Gerais is an institutional body responsible for reviewing and approving research projects to ensure they meet ethical standards and regulations. This committee granted approval for the study under protocol 49368496317.7.0000.5149."},
{"protocol": "The protocol refers to a set of rules and standards established for the ethical conduct of research, specifically in this context, it is associated with the Research Ethics Committee of the Universidade Federal de Minas Gerais."},
{"protocol__is__49368496317_7_0000_5149": "The predicate 'is' signifies the identification or association of the subject (protocol) with a specific code or number, which in this case is a unique identifier assigned by the Research Ethics Committee."},
{"49368496317_7_0000_5149": "The object '49368496317.7.0000.5149' is a unique alphanumeric code assigned to the protocol by the Research Ethics Committee of the Universidade Federal de Minas Gerais, serving as an official identifier for the ethical approval of the study."},
{"this": "This refers to the current study under discussion, which is subject to ethical regulations and has received approval from the Research Ethics Committee of the Universidade Federal de Minas Gerais."},
{"this__is__a_secondary_analysis_of_anonymized_data_stored_in_the_tnmg": "The predicate \"is\" serves as a linking verb that connects the subject (the study) to its nature or characteristic, specifying that it involves a particular type of data analysis."},
{"a_secondary_analysis_of_anonymized_data_stored_in_the_tnmg": "A secondary analysis of anonymized data stored in the TNMG indicates that the study involves reviewing and analyzing data that has already been collected and anonymized, stored within the TNMG (presumably a data repository or network), without the need for new data collection or participant consent."},
{"informed_consent": "Informed consent refers to the process where participants agree to take part in a study after being fully informed about its nature, purpose, and potential risks. In this context, it was not sought from participants due to the secondary analysis of anonymized data."},
{"informed_consent__was_not_required_by__the_research_ethics_committee_for_the_present_study": "The phrase 'was not required by' indicates that the Research Ethics Committee did not mandate the collection of informed consent for the study in question, given the specific circumstances of the research."},
{"the_research_ethics_committee_for_the_present_study": "The Research Ethics Committee for the present study is the body responsible for ensuring that the research complies with ethical standards and regulations. In this case, they determined that informed consent was not necessary for the secondary analysis of anonymized data."},
{"researchers": "Researchers involved in the study conducted by the Universidade Federal de Minas Gerais, who were responsible for analyzing anonymized data stored in the TNMG."},
{"researchers__signed__terms_of_confidentiality_and_data_utilization": "The act of formally agreeing to specific conditions or rules, in this case, related to the handling of confidential information and the utilization of data, as required by the ethical regulations of the study."},
{"terms_of_confidentiality_and_data_utilization": "The formal agreements or documents that outline the conditions under which researchers must maintain confidentiality and properly utilize the data they are analyzing, ensuring compliance with ethical standards."},
{"additional_information": "Additional information refers to supplementary data or details that are provided to enhance the understanding of the main content. In this context, it is specifically related to a scientific paper, indicating that there are extra materials available for readers to explore further."},
{"additional_information__is_available_for__this_paper": "The phrase \"is available for\" indicates that something can be accessed or obtained in relation to another entity. Here, it signifies that the supplementary information can be accessed in connection with the paper, suggesting that readers have the opportunity to delve deeper into the subject matter."},
{"supplementary_information": "Supplementary information refers to additional data, details, or resources that complement the main content of a paper or publication. It is often provided to enhance understanding or to offer further evidence supporting the research findings."},
{"supplementary_information__is_available_at__https_doi_org_10_1038_s41467_020_15432_4": "The phrase \"is available at\" indicates the location or source where the supplementary information can be accessed. It serves as a bridge connecting the supplementary material to its online location, facilitating easy retrieval by interested readers."},
{"correspondence_and_requests_for_materials": "Correspondence and requests for materials refer to any communication or inquiries made regarding the need for specific resources or information.|Here is another description: Correspondence and requests for materials refer to the communication and inquiries made by individuals seeking information or resources. These can include emails, letters, or other forms of contact aimed at obtaining specific materials or clarifications.|Here is another description: Correspondence and requests for materials refer to any communication or inquiries made regarding the acquisition or information about certain materials or resources."},
{"correspondence_and_requests_for_materials__should_be_addressed_to__a_h_r": "The phrase \"should be addressed to\" indicates the proper direction or destination for correspondence and material requests, specifying who is responsible for handling these inquiries."},
{"correspondence_and_requests_for_materials__should_be_addressed_to__t_b_s\u00f6n": "The phrase \"should be addressed to\" indicates the proper direction or destination for correspondence and requests. It specifies who or what entity is responsible for handling these communications, ensuring they reach the appropriate person or department."},
{"t_b_s\u00f6n": "T.B.S\u00f6n. is one of the designated recipients for correspondence and requests for materials. This individual is likely a point of contact within an organization or project, responsible for managing and responding to inquiries related to the materials in question."},
{"correspondence_and_requests_for_materials__should_be_addressed_to__a_l_p_r": "The phrase'should be addressed to' indicates the proper direction or destination for correspondence and requests, specifying who or what entity is responsible for handling these communications."},
{"nature_communications__thanks__rishikesan_kamaleswaran": "The predicate \"thanks\" in this context signifies acknowledgment by Nature Communications towards individuals who have contributed their expertise and time to evaluate and provide feedback on submitted manuscripts as part of the peer review process."},
{"rishikesan_kamaleswaran": "Rishikesan Kamaleswaran is an individual acknowledged by Nature Communications for his contribution to the peer review process, indicating his role as a reviewer who assessed the quality and validity of research submissions."},
{"nature_communications__thanks__wojciech_zareba": "The predicate \"thanks\" in this context signifies acknowledgment and appreciation by Nature Communications towards individuals who have contributed their time and expertise to evaluate and provide feedback on submitted manuscripts as part of the peer review process."},
{"wojciech_zareba": "Wojciech Zareba is an individual acknowledged by Nature Communications for his contribution to the peer review process of a specific work, indicating his role as a subject matter expert who assessed the quality and validity of the research."},
{"nature_communications__thanks__the_other_anonymous_reviewer": "The predicate \"thanks\" in this context signifies acknowledgment and appreciation by Nature Communications towards individuals who have contributed their time and expertise to evaluate and improve the quality of submitted manuscripts through the peer review process."},
{"the_other_anonymous_reviewer": "The other, anonymous, reviewer refers to an unidentified individual who, alongside named reviewers Rishikesan Kamaleswaran and Wojciech Zareba, provided valuable feedback and assessments during the peer review of a specific work published in Nature Communications. Their identity remains undisclosed to maintain the confidentiality and integrity of the peer review process."},
{"peer_reviewer_reports": "Peer reviewer reports refer to the detailed evaluations and feedback provided by experts in the field during the peer review process of a scientific manuscript. These reports play a crucial role in assessing the quality, validity, and significance of the research presented in the manuscript."},
{"peer_reviewer_reports__are__available": "The predicate \"are\" in this context signifies the current state or availability of the peer reviewer reports. It indicates that the reports have been completed and are now accessible for review by relevant parties."},
{"available": "The object \"available\" refers to the status of the peer reviewer reports, meaning they can be accessed and reviewed by those with the appropriate permissions, such as the authors of the manuscript, editors, and potentially the public, depending on the journal's policies."},
{"reprints_and_permission_information": "Reprints and permission information refers to the details and guidelines provided for obtaining reprints of published articles and obtaining permission for various uses of the content."},
{"reprints_and_permission_information__is_available_at__http_www_nature_com_reprints": "The phrase \"is available at\" indicates the location or source where specific information or resources can be accessed, in this case, the website for obtaining reprints and permission details."},
{"http_www_nature_com_reprints": "The URL http://www.nature.com/reprints is the specific web address where users can find reprints and permission information for articles published by Nature, a prominent scientific journal."},
{"springer_nature": "Springer Nature is a major publisher in the fields of science, technology, and medicine, known for its extensive range of academic journals, books, and other scholarly resources."},
